1
00:00:47,547 --> 00:00:49,007
(This film is a work of fiction)

2
00:00:49,090 --> 00:00:50,592
(Any resemblance
to real people, places,)

3
00:00:50,675 --> 00:00:52,218
(or organizations is coincidental)

4
00:00:55,054 --> 00:00:56,806
(Sgt. Seo Jae-hyuk)

5
00:01:00,727 --> 00:01:02,519
(Undercover Assignment)

6
00:01:02,603 --> 00:01:03,771
(Report on the Chilseong Gang)

7
00:01:04,814 --> 00:01:05,522
(Superior Busted for Corruption)

8
00:01:05,606 --> 00:01:06,899
(Operation Failed)

9
00:01:08,109 --> 00:01:10,028
(Demoted)

10
00:01:10,778 --> 00:01:12,196
(Suspect Arrested)

11
00:01:12,697 --> 00:01:13,364
(Suspect Crapped Himself)

12
00:01:17,118 --> 00:01:18,453
(Suspect on the Run)

13
00:01:20,538 --> 00:01:21,956
(Reassigned to the Countryside)

14
00:01:25,126 --> 00:01:27,754
(Demoted Again?)

15
00:01:27,837 --> 00:01:30,840
(Gym)

16
00:01:30,923 --> 00:01:33,802
(The Ultimate Duo)

17
00:01:33,885 --> 00:01:35,970
Yong-man!

18
00:01:42,685 --> 00:01:44,312
Yong-man!

19
00:01:44,896 --> 00:01:46,940
Dang, perfect timing!

20
00:01:47,023 --> 00:01:48,399
I was starving.

21
00:01:50,651 --> 00:01:52,487
Why aren't you eating?
Go on, eat.

22
00:01:58,034 --> 00:01:59,536
Aren't you going to eat?

23
00:01:59,619 --> 00:02:00,412
Bowl's empty?

24
00:02:00,495 --> 00:02:01,537
Allow me.

25
00:02:03,580 --> 00:02:04,874
Here.

26
00:02:04,957 --> 00:02:05,583
Hot!

27
00:02:05,666 --> 00:02:06,668
Goddammit!

28
00:02:06,751 --> 00:02:07,669
Towel!

29
00:02:07,752 --> 00:02:09,086
Oh no, that's hot!

30
00:02:12,423 --> 00:02:13,508
You okay?

31
00:02:13,591 --> 00:02:15,051
Goddammit!

32
00:02:15,134 --> 00:02:18,346
No need to swear at me,
I'm sorry...

33
00:02:19,263 --> 00:02:20,557
Is my girl here?

34
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:22,600
Why is everyone up in arms?

35
00:02:23,518 --> 00:02:24,811
Sgt. Seo is here.

36
00:02:24,894 --> 00:02:26,145
Yong-man.

37
00:02:27,021 --> 00:02:27,814
Under investigation, eh?

38
00:02:27,897 --> 00:02:29,732
Things got a little messy.

39
00:02:30,691 --> 00:02:34,654
I had a drink a few days ago
at my regular bar.

40
00:02:34,737 --> 00:02:36,906
And I found an envelope
in my pocket when I got home.

41
00:02:36,989 --> 00:02:40,076
It felt super off,
so I ran back to return it,

42
00:02:40,159 --> 00:02:41,328
but the bar was closed.

43
00:02:41,411 --> 00:02:44,622
Next day, some jerk filed
a complaint with Internal Affairs.

44
00:02:44,705 --> 00:02:46,499
You're royally fooled, man.

45
00:02:46,582 --> 00:02:47,876
That was you, wasn't it?

46
00:02:47,959 --> 00:02:49,419
You set me up, didn't you?

47
00:02:52,547 --> 00:02:54,632
If you get fired,
come drive a cab for me.

48
00:02:54,715 --> 00:02:55,800
I'll pay minimum wage.

49
00:02:55,883 --> 00:02:56,759
You serious?

50
00:02:57,259 --> 00:02:59,679
But I can't be a cabbie at my age,
I'll be your coach instead.

51
00:02:59,762 --> 00:03:00,472
Pay me more.

52
00:03:00,555 --> 00:03:01,973
Coach?

53
00:03:02,056 --> 00:03:03,892
You'd get your butt kicked.

54
00:03:03,975 --> 00:03:04,601
Yeah?

55
00:03:04,684 --> 00:03:06,144
How about we spar, then?

56
00:03:06,894 --> 00:03:07,896
One-on-one.

57
00:03:07,979 --> 00:03:09,522
Shall we? Alright.

58
00:03:10,106 --> 00:03:13,360
Before you get a beating,
just spill it.

59
00:03:13,443 --> 00:03:14,235
It was you, right?

60
00:03:14,318 --> 00:03:19,031
Don't start whining
after I beat you.

61
00:03:20,283 --> 00:03:22,369
Okay, peace!

62
00:03:22,452 --> 00:03:23,828
Peace! Let's go!

63
00:03:33,045 --> 00:03:33,921
Stop!

64
00:03:35,923 --> 00:03:36,716
Call the ambulance!

65
00:03:36,799 --> 00:03:38,676
Ambulance, goddammit!

66
00:03:43,890 --> 00:03:46,226
Is he really 150th-dan black belt?

67
00:03:46,309 --> 00:03:47,560
It sounds weird...

68
00:03:47,643 --> 00:03:49,061
Right? There's no such thing...

69
00:03:50,813 --> 00:03:52,106
Let's head inside.

70
00:03:53,232 --> 00:03:54,776
He didn't need to
break the window.

71
00:03:54,859 --> 00:03:55,943
Head inside.

72
00:03:57,695 --> 00:03:58,529
Captain!

73
00:03:59,697 --> 00:04:01,073
Shut the hell up!

74
00:04:01,866 --> 00:04:03,159
What's this?

75
00:04:03,242 --> 00:04:04,369
Isn't this weed?

76
00:04:04,452 --> 00:04:05,203
Weed?

77
00:04:05,286 --> 00:04:06,704
Yo, Yong-man!

78
00:04:06,787 --> 00:04:08,206
Isn't this weed?

79
00:04:08,289 --> 00:04:10,291
You son of a gun,
that's not my weed!

80
00:04:10,374 --> 00:04:12,544
Then is it my weed, punk?

81
00:04:12,627 --> 00:04:15,672
You really dabble in everything,
even weed!

82
00:04:15,755 --> 00:04:16,464
I'm really sorry, okay?

83
00:04:16,547 --> 00:04:17,799
No, Mr. Yong-man, I'm sorry.

84
00:04:17,881 --> 00:04:20,551
You'll have to get a drug test.

85
00:04:23,345 --> 00:04:24,597
Feel better now?

86
00:04:24,679 --> 00:04:25,890
I told you we should go with meth.

87
00:04:25,973 --> 00:04:27,350
Where am I supposed to get meth?

88
00:04:27,433 --> 00:04:29,436
Can't a police captain
get some meth?

89
00:04:29,518 --> 00:04:32,104
He'll get a slap on the wrist!
It's like a prank!

90
00:04:33,814 --> 00:04:35,024
What about the tip-off case?

91
00:04:35,691 --> 00:04:37,193
I pulled some strings.

92
00:04:37,276 --> 00:04:38,862
It'll just go away.

93
00:04:38,945 --> 00:04:39,820
It will?

94
00:04:40,321 --> 00:04:42,782
No, it didn't work out.

95
00:04:43,282 --> 00:04:45,785
Whatever, you didn't
even do anything.

96
00:04:48,079 --> 00:04:48,705
Nothing ever works out.

97
00:04:48,788 --> 00:04:51,624
Hey, got some good news though.

98
00:04:52,625 --> 00:04:54,752
Ever heard of Kim Joong-ho?

99
00:04:54,835 --> 00:04:55,837
Who?

100
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:57,588
Kim Joong-ho.

101
00:04:59,756 --> 00:05:01,843
You know Youngjin Foods, right?

102
00:05:01,926 --> 00:05:04,970
He's the only son
of their chairman.

103
00:05:05,054 --> 00:05:07,807
He inherited $20 million
from his grandpa.

104
00:05:08,849 --> 00:05:12,145
But he's got no interest
in running the company.

105
00:05:12,228 --> 00:05:14,689
What's that thing, “influenza”?

106
00:05:14,772 --> 00:05:15,857
Influ-what?

107
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:17,859
The thing where
you're popular online.

108
00:05:17,941 --> 00:05:19,777
Influencer! Influencer!

109
00:05:19,860 --> 00:05:21,070
You're so thick...

110
00:05:22,947 --> 00:05:26,784
Anyway, this punk bragged
about his high IQ online,

111
00:05:26,867 --> 00:05:28,953
and got into a fight with people.

112
00:05:29,036 --> 00:05:31,664
He made a bet for $30,000,

113
00:05:31,747 --> 00:05:33,749
that he'd pass the police exam
in two months.

114
00:05:34,458 --> 00:05:37,545
Then he passed with top scores
on both rounds.

115
00:05:37,628 --> 00:05:38,879
Jesus...

116
00:05:39,505 --> 00:05:41,381
I barely scraped through mine.

117
00:05:41,465 --> 00:05:45,678
But this idiot decided
to really try being a cop.

118
00:05:46,262 --> 00:05:49,766
The moment he got assigned,
he started posting selfies.

119
00:05:49,849 --> 00:05:51,976
He blew up on Instagram,

120
00:05:52,059 --> 00:05:54,771
known as the cop
who drives a Lambo.

121
00:05:54,854 --> 00:05:59,191
People even came to his precinct
to take selfies with him.

122
00:05:59,275 --> 00:06:00,985
All that fuss caused a scene,

123
00:06:01,068 --> 00:06:04,072
and it reached the higher-ups.

124
00:06:04,155 --> 00:06:07,366
The Commissioner got pissed
and sent him away immediately.

125
00:06:08,159 --> 00:06:11,538
Of all places, he sent him
to our precinct, to us!

126
00:06:11,621 --> 00:06:13,623
Do you know how I got
from being

127
00:06:13,706 --> 00:06:15,708
a farmer's son to
sitting in this chair?

128
00:06:15,791 --> 00:06:17,585
Less than five years
to retirement,

129
00:06:17,667 --> 00:06:19,587
and I've got to clean up
after some rich kid?

130
00:06:19,670 --> 00:06:21,672
Just fire the guy already.

131
00:06:22,465 --> 00:06:23,424
How, exactly?

132
00:06:23,506 --> 00:06:27,428
Sgt. Seo here is best
at bullying his subordinates.

133
00:06:27,511 --> 00:06:29,179
Yeah?

134
00:06:29,263 --> 00:06:32,976
If I make Kim Joong-ho
hand in his resignation...

135
00:06:33,059 --> 00:06:33,977
If you do...

136
00:06:34,060 --> 00:06:37,105
Will you get Internal Affairs
off my back?

137
00:06:37,188 --> 00:06:38,564
What did you say?

138
00:07:07,927 --> 00:07:09,095
Salute!

139
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:12,014
That little punk.

140
00:07:14,225 --> 00:07:15,101
Alright, deal.

141
00:07:15,184 --> 00:07:17,437
Can you absolutely get this done?

142
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:20,064
I'm the face of demotions
and resignations.

143
00:07:20,147 --> 00:07:24,026
I'll work hard to make it happen.

144
00:07:31,409 --> 00:07:32,660
Be thorough, got it?

145
00:07:32,743 --> 00:07:35,872
Shouldn't you just take it to
a professional car wash?

146
00:07:35,955 --> 00:07:37,790
You got money to burn?

147
00:07:37,873 --> 00:07:39,292
Right, you do.

148
00:07:39,375 --> 00:07:41,210
It's a patrol car, man.

149
00:07:41,293 --> 00:07:43,879
Comms, electronics, etc.

150
00:07:44,463 --> 00:07:45,965
Outsiders should never touch them.

151
00:07:46,048 --> 00:07:47,508
Be thorough.

152
00:08:00,938 --> 00:08:03,191
No need for hydrophobic coating?

153
00:08:03,274 --> 00:08:04,733
Where did
all this stuff come from?

154
00:08:04,817 --> 00:08:05,902
I had them in my car.

155
00:08:05,985 --> 00:08:09,363
I detailed the general's car
every day for a year in the army.

156
00:08:11,365 --> 00:08:12,533
Is that so?

157
00:08:12,616 --> 00:08:14,035
So is it done now?

158
00:08:14,118 --> 00:08:15,077
What?

159
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:18,038
No, it's not over yet.

160
00:08:19,957 --> 00:08:21,250
Here they come.

161
00:08:23,084 --> 00:08:24,754
They went out on
community support,

162
00:08:24,837 --> 00:08:26,923
another couple will come in.

163
00:08:27,006 --> 00:08:28,007
Make them spotless.

164
00:08:28,089 --> 00:08:30,218
- Let's get off!
- Make sure they're clean.

165
00:08:30,301 --> 00:08:32,261
It's supposed to rain tomorrow.

166
00:08:34,889 --> 00:08:36,682
Isn't this a little too intense
for his first day?

167
00:08:37,641 --> 00:08:39,394
Playing the good cop now?

168
00:08:39,477 --> 00:08:40,478
A case.

169
00:08:40,560 --> 00:08:41,771
What is it?

170
00:08:41,854 --> 00:08:43,147
Theft.

171
00:08:44,023 --> 00:08:45,358
Sgt. Kim.

172
00:08:45,441 --> 00:08:46,983
Your first case on the beat.

173
00:08:47,067 --> 00:08:49,779
They stole the church donation,

174
00:08:49,862 --> 00:08:51,322
$48...

175
00:08:52,031 --> 00:08:53,324
and 70 cents?

176
00:09:00,623 --> 00:09:03,709
You came to the church
at 7 a.m. this morning,

177
00:09:03,793 --> 00:09:05,712
and found the donation box,

178
00:09:05,795 --> 00:09:09,382
two speakers and an amp missing?

179
00:09:09,464 --> 00:09:11,217
Yes, that's right.

180
00:09:11,842 --> 00:09:14,178
Petty thieves like this
are tough to catch.

181
00:09:16,972 --> 00:09:17,973
Hey.

182
00:09:18,474 --> 00:09:20,977
No selfies at the crime scene.

183
00:09:21,060 --> 00:09:22,562
I'm documenting the scene, sir.

184
00:09:22,645 --> 00:09:23,563
Documenting?

185
00:09:23,646 --> 00:09:25,148
What the hell do you know?

186
00:09:25,231 --> 00:09:26,733
I think I know where
he's holed up.

187
00:09:26,816 --> 00:09:28,651
Why the hell are you playing

188
00:09:28,733 --> 00:09:30,445
crime genius
in front of the pastor?

189
00:09:30,528 --> 00:09:34,406
In a town this small,
finding a petty thief is obvious.

190
00:09:34,490 --> 00:09:35,574
Obvious?

191
00:09:39,203 --> 00:09:40,996
What if you can't find him?

192
00:09:41,831 --> 00:09:42,832
I'll give you my car.

193
00:09:42,915 --> 00:09:43,791
What?

194
00:09:46,459 --> 00:09:48,212
I said I'll give you my car.

195
00:09:51,423 --> 00:09:52,091
For real?

196
00:09:52,174 --> 00:09:53,468
What if I catch him?

197
00:09:53,551 --> 00:09:55,094
I'll call you “sir” from here on.

198
00:09:55,177 --> 00:09:56,804
Until you quit the force.

199
00:09:57,471 --> 00:09:59,390
Okay, deal! Let's move out.

200
00:09:59,473 --> 00:10:00,474
Good.

201
00:10:02,893 --> 00:10:06,147
Let me check
the used market prices.

202
00:10:06,230 --> 00:10:07,899
Do motels nearby have internet?

203
00:10:07,982 --> 00:10:09,275
Not here.

204
00:10:09,358 --> 00:10:10,860
Point me to an internet cafe.

205
00:10:10,943 --> 00:10:12,195
The biggest one around.

206
00:10:12,278 --> 00:10:13,153
What for?

207
00:10:13,946 --> 00:10:16,073
If the door was opened with a key,
it's a first-timer.

208
00:10:16,156 --> 00:10:18,367
If it was busted with a crowbar,
it's someone experienced.

209
00:10:18,450 --> 00:10:21,245
This looks like a crowbar job.

210
00:10:21,328 --> 00:10:23,498
If an experienced guy has
the loot, what would he do?

211
00:10:23,581 --> 00:10:26,375
I'd post it online and sell it
in a heartbeat.

212
00:10:26,458 --> 00:10:30,045
But if the motel here
has no internet,

213
00:10:30,629 --> 00:10:31,839
then it's the internet cafe.

214
00:10:31,922 --> 00:10:33,299
You watched too many movies.

215
00:10:33,382 --> 00:10:36,844
In movies, the suspect's always
exactly where you expect, huh?

216
00:10:36,927 --> 00:10:38,679
Lead the way, please.

217
00:10:38,762 --> 00:10:39,972
Go straight.

218
00:10:56,906 --> 00:10:58,156
Aren't you coming?

219
00:10:59,533 --> 00:11:01,202
Did you sleep through
police academy?

220
00:11:01,285 --> 00:11:02,870
Rule when two cops
chase a suspect:

221
00:11:02,953 --> 00:11:05,956
one chases, the other cuts off
the escape route. No?

222
00:11:15,632 --> 00:11:18,218
My luck's finally turning.

223
00:11:25,726 --> 00:11:26,727
Huh?

224
00:11:32,191 --> 00:11:33,108
No way!

225
00:11:33,192 --> 00:11:34,360
Why are these here?

226
00:11:42,368 --> 00:11:43,535
Christ...

227
00:11:58,092 --> 00:11:58,634
Who are you?

228
00:11:58,717 --> 00:11:59,635
- Hide!
- What?

229
00:12:07,726 --> 00:12:08,644
- He's coming.
- What?

230
00:12:08,727 --> 00:12:10,145
Drive! Now!

231
00:12:12,773 --> 00:12:13,524
Wait...

232
00:12:16,193 --> 00:12:18,362
Sir! Sir!

233
00:12:18,445 --> 00:12:20,113
Sir! Stop, jerk!

234
00:12:20,197 --> 00:12:22,158
He's running,
he's coming after us.

235
00:12:22,241 --> 00:12:23,492
Who are you?!

236
00:12:23,575 --> 00:12:25,161
Ask later, just floor it.

237
00:12:25,244 --> 00:12:27,580
If that guy catches up,
you're so dead.

238
00:12:27,663 --> 00:12:29,373
Who the hell are you?

239
00:12:29,456 --> 00:12:29,957
Hey! Front! Front!

240
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:31,125
Dammit...

241
00:12:31,208 --> 00:12:32,042
Goddamn...

242
00:12:41,385 --> 00:12:42,553
Don't move!

243
00:12:42,636 --> 00:12:43,679
Hold still!

244
00:12:44,887 --> 00:12:45,389
It's about time.

245
00:12:45,472 --> 00:12:46,557
How'd you get here?

246
00:12:46,640 --> 00:12:48,100
What do you mean, how?

247
00:12:48,183 --> 00:12:50,060
I covered the escape route.

248
00:12:50,144 --> 00:12:51,729
Toss him in the car.

249
00:12:52,604 --> 00:12:53,397
Prick!

250
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:55,399
You need to drive better!

251
00:12:56,191 --> 00:12:57,401
Toss him in!

252
00:13:20,132 --> 00:13:21,759
How was he?

253
00:13:21,842 --> 00:13:25,512
For a rookie, he's not
completely hopeless.

254
00:13:25,596 --> 00:13:26,805
Come on.

255
00:13:26,889 --> 00:13:28,391
He caught one little guppy.

256
00:13:28,474 --> 00:13:30,017
Might not be a guppy.

257
00:13:32,144 --> 00:13:32,978
What's up?

258
00:13:33,687 --> 00:13:35,147
Isn't this bloodstain?

259
00:13:35,230 --> 00:13:37,066
It's dry, it looks very old.

260
00:13:38,608 --> 00:13:39,735
Check out the handle.

261
00:13:39,818 --> 00:13:41,237
Was this thing filed down?

262
00:13:41,320 --> 00:13:43,613
Fits in your hand,
perfect for a quick strike.

263
00:13:44,156 --> 00:13:45,116
A sudden whack!

264
00:13:45,199 --> 00:13:47,743
This one's a big fish!

265
00:13:47,826 --> 00:13:49,161
Get some work done for once?

266
00:13:49,244 --> 00:13:51,414
Please, Sergeant.

267
00:13:51,497 --> 00:13:53,124
Just kill this sinner already.

268
00:13:53,207 --> 00:13:54,834
You thieving prick!

269
00:13:54,917 --> 00:13:58,004
You couldn't find anywhere else
to steal from but a church?

270
00:13:58,087 --> 00:13:58,962
You damn thief!

271
00:13:59,505 --> 00:14:01,090
Guys like you
don't deserve to die.

272
00:14:01,173 --> 00:14:03,843
You shouldn't just burn in hell.

273
00:14:03,926 --> 00:14:05,553
You ought to be boiled alive
in a cauldron!

274
00:14:05,636 --> 00:14:07,096
Thieving prick!

275
00:14:07,930 --> 00:14:09,098
Do you even go to church?

276
00:14:09,181 --> 00:14:10,891
My father was a pastor
at a small church!

277
00:14:10,974 --> 00:14:13,102
You know how much
a small church pastor makes?

278
00:14:13,185 --> 00:14:15,521
$50 a week, $200 a month.

279
00:14:15,604 --> 00:14:18,024
That's $2,000 a year,
you thieving wrinkled punk!

280
00:14:18,107 --> 00:14:19,275
That's enough!

281
00:14:19,358 --> 00:14:20,984
It's $2,400 a year!

282
00:14:21,819 --> 00:14:23,279
Is that right?

283
00:14:23,362 --> 00:14:24,613
Must be nice to be good at math!

284
00:14:24,696 --> 00:14:25,489
You thieving punk!

285
00:14:25,572 --> 00:14:27,241
- Somebody help me!
- Captain, what are you doing?!

286
00:14:27,324 --> 00:14:27,950
Please help!

287
00:14:28,033 --> 00:14:29,660
What are you doing?

288
00:14:29,743 --> 00:14:31,078
You can't do this!

289
00:14:32,412 --> 00:14:33,289
I'm going to kill him!

290
00:14:33,372 --> 00:14:34,540
Watch out!

291
00:14:36,416 --> 00:14:37,626
Wait a second!

292
00:14:37,709 --> 00:14:38,419
What are you doing?!

293
00:14:38,502 --> 00:14:40,546
Get Captain out of here!

294
00:14:40,629 --> 00:14:41,630
Get him out!

295
00:14:41,713 --> 00:14:42,298
Son of a gun!

296
00:14:42,381 --> 00:14:44,008
Get him out at once!
It's dangerous!

297
00:14:44,091 --> 00:14:47,386
Who's teaching who?
Let go of me!

298
00:14:57,437 --> 00:14:58,522
Are you okay?

299
00:14:58,605 --> 00:15:00,274
Why a church out of all places?

300
00:15:00,357 --> 00:15:01,734
Not very professional of you.

301
00:15:01,817 --> 00:15:03,694
How many priors
do you have for this?

302
00:15:03,777 --> 00:15:07,782
That's minimum three years
for aggravated theft.

303
00:15:07,865 --> 00:15:10,493
Three years for $48.70.

304
00:15:10,576 --> 00:15:11,577
Unbelievable...

305
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:14,121
If it were me, I'd drown myself
in that paper cup.

306
00:15:14,204 --> 00:15:17,749
I thought there'd be more,
this is embarrassing for me too.

307
00:15:18,250 --> 00:15:20,294
Anyway, Chang-su.

308
00:15:20,377 --> 00:15:24,131
Your old turf was Seoul, right?

309
00:15:24,214 --> 00:15:25,633
You give off that Seoul vibe.

310
00:15:25,716 --> 00:15:28,344
Sergeant,
you sure can read people.

311
00:15:28,427 --> 00:15:30,345
Not really, it's on your record.

312
00:15:32,431 --> 00:15:34,391
I'm actually a Gangnam native.

313
00:15:34,474 --> 00:15:35,601
Gangnam?

314
00:15:35,684 --> 00:15:39,438
I had tabs on five hostess bars
in Yeoksam alone three years ago.

315
00:15:39,521 --> 00:15:42,524
Damn, you were
rolling in it back then.

316
00:15:43,066 --> 00:15:46,445
So what, you hit up
those “10%” joints too?

317
00:15:49,239 --> 00:15:51,033
Don't even mention it.

318
00:15:51,116 --> 00:15:52,118
10%...

319
00:15:52,201 --> 00:15:54,328
- Sergeant.
- Yeah?

320
00:15:54,411 --> 00:15:56,413
- You know what “10%” is?
- Of course I do.

321
00:15:56,496 --> 00:15:58,290
Top 10% in looks, right?

322
00:15:58,373 --> 00:15:59,667
Come on, that's not it at all.

323
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:02,711
They take 10% off the girls' tips.

324
00:16:02,794 --> 00:16:04,713
Is that so?

325
00:16:04,796 --> 00:16:06,006
I see.

326
00:16:06,590 --> 00:16:10,136
So how the hell did you
end up like this?

327
00:16:10,219 --> 00:16:11,637
Jesus Christ...

328
00:16:12,721 --> 00:16:18,060
It was around this time last year.

329
00:16:18,769 --> 00:16:21,313
I got drunk and
took the wrong cab,

330
00:16:21,396 --> 00:16:24,233
ended up somewhere in Gangnam...

331
00:16:24,316 --> 00:16:29,029
Broke and wasted,
I thought, ‘Whatever,

332
00:16:29,112 --> 00:16:31,823
I'll just hit up some cheap bar,
drink and dash.'

333
00:16:33,533 --> 00:16:35,578
But the girl working there
was gorgeous.

334
00:16:35,661 --> 00:16:36,787
Yeah?

335
00:16:38,038 --> 00:16:38,747
And then?

336
00:16:38,830 --> 00:16:41,041
So I tried to hit on her.

337
00:16:41,124 --> 00:16:44,253
But that wench
treated me like trash!

338
00:16:44,336 --> 00:16:45,045
That wench!

339
00:16:45,128 --> 00:16:46,672
- I said, “I've got money!”
- Yeah!

340
00:16:46,755 --> 00:16:49,383
But she kept mouthing off,
pissing me off more!

341
00:16:49,466 --> 00:16:50,676
So you hit her with a hammer?

342
00:16:50,759 --> 00:16:53,887
I didn't mean to do it...

343
00:17:00,978 --> 00:17:02,812
This was in your bag.

344
00:17:03,647 --> 00:17:04,982
See the dried blood?

345
00:17:05,065 --> 00:17:09,403
Then you wandered around
some backwater town,

346
00:17:10,153 --> 00:17:12,697
robbing churches whenever
you ran out of cash?

347
00:17:12,781 --> 00:17:13,991
No...

348
00:17:15,450 --> 00:17:18,162
That story wasn't about me.

349
00:17:18,245 --> 00:17:21,915
I don't even know where
those Gangnam bars are.

350
00:17:25,877 --> 00:17:27,587
Heard of the forensics lab?

351
00:17:28,171 --> 00:17:30,257
They'll have the results
in two days.

352
00:17:30,340 --> 00:17:30,925
What's it going to be?

353
00:17:31,008 --> 00:17:33,135
Confess now and sleep soundly?

354
00:17:33,218 --> 00:17:35,763
Or stay up for
three nights with me

355
00:17:35,846 --> 00:17:38,307
until your bladder explodes?

356
00:17:41,851 --> 00:17:42,728
Man...

357
00:17:45,314 --> 00:17:46,523
Jesus! You scared
the crap out of me!

358
00:17:46,606 --> 00:17:48,567
What are you doing?

359
00:17:48,649 --> 00:17:51,110
- It's pointless, buddy!
- Dammit!

360
00:17:51,194 --> 00:17:52,488
You tried to entrap me!

361
00:17:52,571 --> 00:17:54,364
- Don't move!
- Calm down!

362
00:17:59,703 --> 00:18:01,205
No matter how you slice it,

363
00:18:01,288 --> 00:18:02,956
wasn't that
a pretty slick confession?

364
00:18:03,749 --> 00:18:05,542
Never seen
anything like it, right?

365
00:18:05,625 --> 00:18:07,878
You've barely seen anything.

366
00:18:08,795 --> 00:18:10,965
I get it, so can you please
stop talking now?

367
00:18:11,048 --> 00:18:13,759
And maybe learn how to use
that taser properly next time.

368
00:18:13,841 --> 00:18:16,386
Did the volts hurt a lot?

369
00:18:17,012 --> 00:18:19,932
A little shock and
you're done being a cop?

370
00:18:20,014 --> 00:18:21,183
Do you want to quit?

371
00:18:21,266 --> 00:18:23,560
Are you not going to
give me my car keys?

372
00:18:24,644 --> 00:18:25,479
Why should I?

373
00:18:25,562 --> 00:18:27,189
Because I caught him.

374
00:18:27,272 --> 00:18:29,149
And I'm the one who cuffed him.

375
00:18:29,232 --> 00:18:30,818
You can barely afford
the gas for that car.

376
00:18:30,901 --> 00:18:32,319
I'm goigng to sell it.

377
00:18:33,070 --> 00:18:34,279
On used market online.

378
00:18:35,447 --> 00:18:36,490
Am I pissing you off?

379
00:18:37,240 --> 00:18:40,285
If you're pissed, you can quit.

380
00:18:43,747 --> 00:18:45,457
So where exactly are we going?

381
00:18:45,540 --> 00:18:47,668
To see the prosecutor in charge.

382
00:18:47,751 --> 00:18:49,168
It's eleven at night.

383
00:18:49,252 --> 00:18:52,798
Some nutcase shot
21 rounds from an air rifle.

384
00:18:52,881 --> 00:18:54,133
For not paying back a debt.

385
00:18:54,216 --> 00:18:57,469
But the prosecutor's
a real hardcore.

386
00:18:57,552 --> 00:18:59,722
She's still digging
through the corpse

387
00:18:59,805 --> 00:19:02,014
herself to find all 21 pellets.

388
00:19:02,766 --> 00:19:03,642
The corpse?

389
00:19:04,559 --> 00:19:05,685
Found another one.

390
00:19:06,311 --> 00:19:07,812
Two bullets left.

391
00:19:08,437 --> 00:19:11,066
It's past midnight already,
are we staying up all night?

392
00:19:11,566 --> 00:19:12,693
Aren't you tired?

393
00:19:12,776 --> 00:19:15,362
Let's be respectful
to the victim here.

394
00:19:15,445 --> 00:19:16,780
Hurry up and find them.

395
00:19:16,863 --> 00:19:17,864
Sure...

396
00:19:21,743 --> 00:19:23,620
I punched once out of anger...

397
00:19:23,703 --> 00:19:26,790
Right now, the suspect's statement
is all you've got.

398
00:19:26,873 --> 00:19:30,793
That's why we came to see you,
to start a proper investigation.

399
00:19:31,503 --> 00:19:32,713
If it's a homicide,

400
00:19:32,796 --> 00:19:33,881
Seoul HQ must've
formed a team already.

401
00:19:33,964 --> 00:19:36,758
But the perp was caught here.

402
00:19:37,509 --> 00:19:39,261
It's our case first.

403
00:19:40,053 --> 00:19:42,305
Found one more.

404
00:19:43,181 --> 00:19:45,184
Let's wrap this up
and talk over dinner.

405
00:19:45,267 --> 00:19:46,185
Sounds great.

406
00:19:46,268 --> 00:19:50,730
The last one's lodged deep inside,
it's going to take some time.

407
00:19:56,653 --> 00:19:57,571
What's with him?

408
00:19:57,654 --> 00:19:59,281
He's our rookie.

409
00:20:01,408 --> 00:20:03,452
He looks familiar...

410
00:20:11,251 --> 00:20:12,210
Ma'am.

411
00:20:13,003 --> 00:20:14,546
It's you, isn't it?

412
00:20:14,629 --> 00:20:15,422
What is?

413
00:20:15,505 --> 00:20:18,133
Seojin Girls' High,
Osaka field trip.

414
00:20:20,218 --> 00:20:21,261
Nope.

415
00:20:22,512 --> 00:20:23,763
I'm sure it is.

416
00:20:26,224 --> 00:20:27,976
I said it's not!

417
00:20:28,059 --> 00:20:29,853
Come on, you confessed
to me back then.

418
00:20:29,936 --> 00:20:33,148
I rejected you, and you cried
your eyes out, Kang Mi-ju.

419
00:20:33,231 --> 00:20:34,942
It wasn't me.

420
00:20:35,024 --> 00:20:36,777
Must be someone else
with the same name.

421
00:20:36,860 --> 00:20:37,860
Nah, it was you.

422
00:20:37,944 --> 00:20:39,112
I said no!

423
00:20:42,324 --> 00:20:44,075
You can't do anything with this.

424
00:20:45,160 --> 00:20:46,328
I'll give you three days.

425
00:20:51,416 --> 00:20:52,542
You idiot!

426
00:20:53,668 --> 00:20:55,712
What kind of cop flirts
with a prosecutor?

427
00:20:55,795 --> 00:20:59,341
I wasn't flirting,
Kang Mi-ju was famous.

428
00:20:59,424 --> 00:21:02,469
She waited for me outside of
school and even my house.

429
00:21:02,552 --> 00:21:04,096
You wouldn't know.

430
00:21:04,179 --> 00:21:05,806
Hey.

431
00:21:05,889 --> 00:21:06,889
Shut up and eat.

432
00:21:20,529 --> 00:21:21,989
Is this really Gangnam?

433
00:21:22,072 --> 00:21:24,283
Do you even know how much
the land here costs?

434
00:21:24,366 --> 00:21:25,451
I know.

435
00:21:25,533 --> 00:21:26,535
Expensive.

436
00:21:31,581 --> 00:21:33,458
I think this is the place.

437
00:21:34,543 --> 00:21:36,086
It's the only place.

438
00:21:37,379 --> 00:21:38,672
The Nest, eh?

439
00:21:38,755 --> 00:21:39,882
(The Nest)

440
00:21:39,965 --> 00:21:41,883
Ma'am, mind if I record this?

441
00:21:44,594 --> 00:21:46,555
When did this place open?

442
00:21:47,472 --> 00:21:49,057
Since the day it opened.

443
00:21:49,139 --> 00:21:50,809
And when was that exactly?

444
00:21:55,272 --> 00:21:56,982
It's not open yet.

445
00:21:57,607 --> 00:21:59,485
Please answer
the question properly.

446
00:21:59,568 --> 00:22:01,487
Sergeant, are you single?

447
00:22:01,570 --> 00:22:02,654
No, I'm not.

448
00:22:02,737 --> 00:22:05,115
And stop asking
irrelevant questions.

449
00:22:05,197 --> 00:22:06,450
Then you're married?

450
00:22:06,533 --> 00:22:07,826
I'm not married.

451
00:22:07,908 --> 00:22:10,162
Then it's complicated,
am I right?

452
00:22:10,245 --> 00:22:12,122
- Pardon?
- Oh boy...

453
00:22:12,872 --> 00:22:14,416
What's your name?

454
00:22:14,499 --> 00:22:15,667
Lee Hwa-ran.

455
00:22:15,750 --> 00:22:16,793
And your age?

456
00:22:16,876 --> 00:22:18,128
Thirty-something.

457
00:22:18,211 --> 00:22:19,254
Come on.

458
00:22:19,337 --> 00:22:21,507
More like fifty, right?

459
00:22:21,590 --> 00:22:22,799
I am not!

460
00:22:22,882 --> 00:22:25,636
Was this place named after
that Namjin song?

461
00:22:25,719 --> 00:22:27,888
I remember hearing it as a kid.

462
00:22:27,971 --> 00:22:28,972
You're older than me?

463
00:22:29,055 --> 00:22:30,849
I've only been here two years.

464
00:22:30,932 --> 00:22:33,310
Is that so?

465
00:22:34,101 --> 00:22:36,897
Then you were here
around this time last year.

466
00:22:36,980 --> 00:22:39,149
Something happened here,
didn't it?

467
00:22:40,649 --> 00:22:42,277
A murder.

468
00:22:42,360 --> 00:22:44,029
You need to answer honestly.

469
00:22:44,654 --> 00:22:47,115
Something terrible happened
to one of my girls.

470
00:22:47,991 --> 00:22:49,368
The victim's name?

471
00:22:49,451 --> 00:22:50,535
Min-a.

472
00:22:51,244 --> 00:22:52,120
Lee Min-a.

473
00:22:52,203 --> 00:22:54,665
Someone died and you still
kept this place open?

474
00:22:54,748 --> 00:22:57,334
Then what? Close after dropping
$30,000 on the lease?

475
00:22:57,417 --> 00:22:59,711
Exactly. Was she supposed
to shut it down?

476
00:23:00,670 --> 00:23:03,257
Must've been pretty rough.

477
00:23:03,340 --> 00:23:06,009
Those Seoul cops couldn't even
catch the guy.

478
00:23:06,760 --> 00:23:08,511
But it's all over now.

479
00:23:09,512 --> 00:23:11,389
We caught that jerk.

480
00:23:13,224 --> 00:23:15,435
Min-a's killer was caught.

481
00:23:15,518 --> 00:23:18,605
He was a regular named
Cho Dong-oh.

482
00:23:18,687 --> 00:23:21,691
They caught him right after and
he's in prison now.

483
00:23:31,701 --> 00:23:32,952
Aren't you getting in?

484
00:23:38,041 --> 00:23:39,543
What are you going to do now?

485
00:23:39,626 --> 00:23:41,252
What else?

486
00:23:41,753 --> 00:23:43,463
Head back and pull some
late nights.

487
00:23:44,130 --> 00:23:45,215
What a letdown.

488
00:23:45,298 --> 00:23:47,341
I thought we'd landed
a cool homicide case.

489
00:23:47,926 --> 00:23:49,260
A cool homicide case?

490
00:23:49,928 --> 00:23:50,762
You think murder's a joke?

491
00:23:50,845 --> 00:23:52,347
You said you were
a seasoned veteran.

492
00:23:52,430 --> 00:23:53,181
Say what?

493
00:23:53,264 --> 00:23:54,891
Does a seasoned veteran
fall for a suspect's lie?

494
00:23:54,974 --> 00:23:56,643
You cocky little...

495
00:23:56,726 --> 00:23:59,646
If you're going to mouth off,
quit right now!

496
00:24:03,066 --> 00:24:04,067
What's that look?

497
00:24:04,149 --> 00:24:05,485
Are you going to
take a swing at me?

498
00:24:09,489 --> 00:24:11,283
You keep telling me to quit.

499
00:24:11,366 --> 00:24:12,783
What's your deal?

500
00:24:12,867 --> 00:24:14,244
Don't like hearing it?

501
00:24:14,327 --> 00:24:16,788
Then quit already
if you hate it so much!

502
00:24:18,415 --> 00:24:19,791
You really want to have a go?

503
00:24:19,874 --> 00:24:21,126
You said you did
martial arts, right?

504
00:24:21,209 --> 00:24:21,793
Yes.

505
00:24:22,752 --> 00:24:24,421
Do you want to spar with me?

506
00:24:24,504 --> 00:24:26,172
Bring it.

507
00:24:38,893 --> 00:24:39,853
Come here, come!

508
00:24:39,936 --> 00:24:40,479
Dammit!

509
00:24:40,562 --> 00:24:42,187
You lose, you quit.

510
00:24:44,733 --> 00:24:46,526
I'll apologize
for underestimating you.

511
00:24:49,487 --> 00:24:50,530
What are you doing?

512
00:24:50,613 --> 00:24:51,907
Feeling dizzy already?

513
00:24:51,990 --> 00:24:54,283
Careful, man,
you could really get hurt.

514
00:24:54,367 --> 00:24:57,412
Underestimate Capoeira,
and you're dead.

515
00:24:58,288 --> 00:24:59,623
Oh yeah?

516
00:24:59,706 --> 00:25:01,040
Let's start with a fist bump.

517
00:25:18,141 --> 00:25:19,559
Hey! Wait, wait, wait!

518
00:25:19,642 --> 00:25:20,268
Wait, wait!

519
00:25:20,351 --> 00:25:21,978
Wait, hold up!

520
00:25:22,979 --> 00:25:25,857
I got a call! A call! Phone!

521
00:25:27,442 --> 00:25:29,319
Hello? Yes!

522
00:25:30,069 --> 00:25:31,697
Something urgent came up.

523
00:25:31,780 --> 00:25:33,072
Alright.

524
00:25:41,372 --> 00:25:42,124
Oh, yes.

525
00:25:42,207 --> 00:25:43,625
You should call it.

526
00:25:46,336 --> 00:25:47,545
You jerk!

527
00:25:48,505 --> 00:25:49,381
Say you lost!

528
00:25:49,464 --> 00:25:50,882
- Say you lost!
- What are you doing at my store?

529
00:25:50,965 --> 00:25:51,800
Say...

530
00:25:53,635 --> 00:25:54,886
Hold on, hold on!

531
00:25:55,386 --> 00:25:57,180
Wait, my phone, jerk!

532
00:25:59,057 --> 00:25:59,891
Prick.

533
00:25:59,974 --> 00:26:01,393
You coward!

534
00:26:01,476 --> 00:26:02,519
Say you lost!

535
00:26:02,601 --> 00:26:03,853
Say you lost!

536
00:26:05,146 --> 00:26:06,481
Say you lost!

537
00:26:08,441 --> 00:26:09,776
Say it.

538
00:26:09,859 --> 00:26:10,902
Hello? Police?

539
00:26:10,985 --> 00:26:13,780
There are a couple of
drink lunatics fighting here!

540
00:26:14,656 --> 00:26:16,533
- Let go of me!
- Say you lost!

541
00:26:16,616 --> 00:26:17,908
Let go of me!

542
00:26:17,992 --> 00:26:19,119
(Seoul Gangnam Police)

543
00:26:19,202 --> 00:26:20,203
I heard a noise, came out

544
00:26:20,286 --> 00:26:21,913
found them drunk
out of their minds,

545
00:26:21,995 --> 00:26:23,832
swinging and rolling
on the ground.

546
00:26:23,915 --> 00:26:25,208
Hey.

547
00:26:25,291 --> 00:26:27,543
You knocked me down,
so you're paying for the damages.

548
00:26:28,628 --> 00:26:31,381
You're the one
who suggested we fight.

549
00:26:34,759 --> 00:26:35,761
Now, this...

550
00:26:35,844 --> 00:26:37,429
Sorry about all this.

551
00:26:37,512 --> 00:26:39,723
We didn't mention it earlier
in front of the lady, but...

552
00:26:39,806 --> 00:26:42,225
Here, sign this paperwork first,

553
00:26:42,308 --> 00:26:43,268
I'm really busy.

554
00:26:43,351 --> 00:26:43,769
Sign this?

555
00:26:43,851 --> 00:26:46,937
Property damage, mutual assault,
drunk and disorderly...

556
00:26:47,021 --> 00:26:47,606
Wait, I...

557
00:26:47,689 --> 00:26:50,066
I talk, then you talk, got it?

558
00:26:50,149 --> 00:26:52,569
You two go cool off in holding,

559
00:26:52,652 --> 00:26:55,197
hold hands, reflect,
kneel if you have to.

560
00:26:55,280 --> 00:26:56,697
We'll talk settlement tomorrow.

561
00:26:56,781 --> 00:26:58,908
Don't you even confirm
victim statements here?

562
00:26:59,492 --> 00:27:02,370
Been in holding before, huh?

563
00:27:02,453 --> 00:27:03,538
You know what to do.

564
00:27:04,205 --> 00:27:07,751
You sign this,
and you too, right here.

565
00:27:07,834 --> 00:27:09,293
Sign on this line.

566
00:27:09,377 --> 00:27:11,379
Who taught this punk manners?

567
00:27:11,462 --> 00:27:12,798
None of your business, jerk.

568
00:27:12,881 --> 00:27:16,718
Show me where the Police Act
says you can talk like that.

569
00:27:16,801 --> 00:27:18,553
Hold him back, man!

570
00:27:20,471 --> 00:27:21,681
Stop it!

571
00:27:22,264 --> 00:27:23,266
Captain.

572
00:27:24,058 --> 00:27:25,018
Enough!

573
00:27:26,644 --> 00:27:27,562
You punks.

574
00:27:28,062 --> 00:27:29,522
What the hell are you doing?

575
00:27:30,940 --> 00:27:33,318
Don't even recognize
fellow officers?

576
00:27:33,401 --> 00:27:34,735
Apologize properly!

577
00:27:34,819 --> 00:27:36,279
It's fine, really.

578
00:27:36,362 --> 00:27:39,197
It's all good,
don't worry about it.

579
00:27:40,116 --> 00:27:41,618
Unbelievable,
fighting among family.

580
00:27:41,701 --> 00:27:44,162
You were with the Major Crimes
at South Precinct?

581
00:27:44,245 --> 00:27:47,749
Yeah, right before I got
transferred to Boeun.

582
00:27:47,832 --> 00:27:49,292
You must know Baek Dae-hoon.

583
00:27:49,375 --> 00:27:50,793
He's my classmate.

584
00:27:50,877 --> 00:27:51,878
Baek Dae-hoon?

585
00:27:53,004 --> 00:27:53,630
Hm?

586
00:27:55,548 --> 00:27:57,133
Baek Dae-hoon?

587
00:27:59,594 --> 00:28:01,679
That clueless thumbsucker.

588
00:28:02,472 --> 00:28:04,724
I used to give him
a hard time back then.

589
00:28:04,807 --> 00:28:05,934
Is that right?

590
00:28:06,643 --> 00:28:09,145
We started out together at East,

591
00:28:09,228 --> 00:28:10,355
I'm a bit older though.

592
00:28:10,438 --> 00:28:12,607
Is that right?

593
00:28:14,233 --> 00:28:16,653
He was our rookie back in Nonsan.

594
00:28:17,820 --> 00:28:18,905
You two close?

595
00:28:18,988 --> 00:28:22,033
Not really, just colleagues.

596
00:28:23,868 --> 00:28:27,497
Still a sergeant
after all these years?

597
00:28:27,580 --> 00:28:28,957
It's not that I stayed
a sergeant long,

598
00:28:29,040 --> 00:28:31,042
I've been up and down the ranks.

599
00:28:31,125 --> 00:28:32,961
Even did a brief stint
as lieutenant.

600
00:28:36,339 --> 00:28:38,091
You're going to
make me tear up.

601
00:28:38,174 --> 00:28:40,802
How many times
did you mess up?

602
00:28:40,885 --> 00:28:42,637
What brings you to Seoul, anyway?

603
00:28:42,720 --> 00:28:45,473
We picked up some petty thief
in our district,

604
00:28:45,974 --> 00:28:48,018
and turns out he'd caused

605
00:28:48,101 --> 00:28:50,019
some trouble here
about a year ago.

606
00:28:51,437 --> 00:28:52,438
Yeah?

607
00:28:52,981 --> 00:28:54,649
Anything I can do to help?

608
00:28:54,732 --> 00:28:56,985
Have you heard of a small bar
called The Nest?

609
00:28:57,068 --> 00:28:58,194
Buddy!

610
00:29:00,071 --> 00:29:00,655
The Nest?

611
00:29:00,738 --> 00:29:01,990
Captain, wasn't that the
Lee Min-a case?

612
00:29:02,073 --> 00:29:03,116
Buddy!

613
00:29:05,785 --> 00:29:07,829
Goddamn rookie.

614
00:29:10,707 --> 00:29:12,584
If you need anything,
just say the word.

615
00:29:12,667 --> 00:29:13,501
Sgt. Park.

616
00:29:13,584 --> 00:29:15,253
He'll help.

617
00:29:15,336 --> 00:29:16,462
Help them out.

618
00:29:17,672 --> 00:29:19,633
Why are we rushing back so fast?

619
00:29:19,716 --> 00:29:21,384
Because it's urgent.

620
00:29:21,467 --> 00:29:23,511
I don't think we got it wrong.

621
00:29:23,594 --> 00:29:24,971
But they already caught the guy.

622
00:29:25,054 --> 00:29:26,389
He was convicted.

623
00:29:26,472 --> 00:29:28,808
Something about them felt off.

624
00:29:28,891 --> 00:29:30,477
Real shady jerks.

625
00:29:30,560 --> 00:29:32,103
What's so suspicious about
being jerks?

626
00:29:32,186 --> 00:29:34,648
If the killer's really caught,

627
00:29:34,731 --> 00:29:36,900
then it means Kang Chang-su lied.

628
00:29:36,983 --> 00:29:38,485
But why'd a petty thief
who robs churches

629
00:29:38,568 --> 00:29:41,279
lie about a murder
he didn't even commit?

630
00:29:45,491 --> 00:29:46,785
Who are you calling?

631
00:29:46,868 --> 00:29:48,119
The prosecutor.

632
00:29:48,703 --> 00:29:50,080
Now?

633
00:29:50,163 --> 00:29:52,290
When you meet a woman you like,

634
00:29:52,373 --> 00:29:53,875
but can't get her number
in three minutes,

635
00:29:53,958 --> 00:29:55,626
it's game over.

636
00:29:56,377 --> 00:29:57,796
What the hell does that mean?

637
00:29:57,879 --> 00:29:59,673
You mean you like her?

638
00:29:59,756 --> 00:30:01,883
Ma'am, it's Kim Joong-ho.

639
00:30:01,966 --> 00:30:03,093
What's going on?

640
00:30:03,176 --> 00:30:05,219
They caught a perp in Seoul,

641
00:30:05,803 --> 00:30:08,264
but these idiots
nabbed the wrong guy.

642
00:30:10,767 --> 00:30:15,188
Seoul Gangnam Case No. 1137, 2018.

643
00:30:15,271 --> 00:30:17,148
Interrogation record
of Cho Dong-oh,

644
00:30:17,231 --> 00:30:19,401
a suspect in the Lee Min-a murder.

645
00:30:19,484 --> 00:30:22,028
Come on, just one kiss.

646
00:30:22,111 --> 00:30:23,947
No one's around!
Just one kiss!

647
00:30:24,030 --> 00:30:27,325
“While drinking with her,
I got into an argument,

648
00:30:27,408 --> 00:30:30,662
I lost it before I
even realized it...

649
00:30:30,745 --> 00:30:31,329
You wench!

650
00:30:31,412 --> 00:30:33,540
I hit her with a bottle.

651
00:30:33,623 --> 00:30:38,252
When I realized what happened,
she had already stopped breathing.

652
00:30:39,003 --> 00:30:42,173
I was too drunk to think straight,

653
00:30:42,256 --> 00:30:45,843
so I dumped the body nearby
and went home.”

654
00:30:47,386 --> 00:30:49,347
This is Kang Chang-su's
interrogation record.

655
00:30:49,430 --> 00:30:51,307
“June 17th, 2018.

656
00:30:51,390 --> 00:30:55,937
I took a cab to Yangjae district
and went into a bar.

657
00:30:56,687 --> 00:30:59,941
I asked for a drink,
but the girl didn't say a word.”

658
00:31:00,024 --> 00:31:00,942
We're closed!

659
00:31:01,025 --> 00:31:04,070
Whatever, it's raining,
I need to have a drink.

660
00:31:04,153 --> 00:31:06,448
I said we're closed!

661
00:31:06,531 --> 00:31:07,866
I've got money!

662
00:31:07,949 --> 00:31:10,452
“Even after I said I've got money,
she ignored me.

663
00:31:10,535 --> 00:31:13,663
So I got pissed and shoved her,

664
00:31:13,746 --> 00:31:17,709
and it seemed she hit her head
on the table when she fell.”

665
00:31:17,792 --> 00:31:19,794
However, we believe
the actual weapon was

666
00:31:19,877 --> 00:31:23,840
a bloodstained hammer
found in his car.

667
00:31:25,967 --> 00:31:30,096
So that's the only reason
Gangnam PD pinned it on Cho?

668
00:31:30,179 --> 00:31:31,848
No, not just that.

669
00:31:31,931 --> 00:31:34,059
He didn't have
an alibi that night,

670
00:31:34,142 --> 00:31:35,435
and most importantly,

671
00:31:35,518 --> 00:31:39,189
there was an eyewitness.

672
00:31:39,272 --> 00:31:40,565
An eyewitness?

673
00:31:40,648 --> 00:31:43,485
The victim's sister,
Lee Jin-kyung.

674
00:31:43,568 --> 00:31:45,820
This is tricky.

675
00:31:46,863 --> 00:31:49,365
Let's just pass
the whole case to Seoul.

676
00:31:49,866 --> 00:31:51,576
They'll take care of it.

677
00:31:51,659 --> 00:31:52,952
Exactly.

678
00:31:53,035 --> 00:31:55,997
If we start poking around,
Gangnam PD will take it as

679
00:31:56,080 --> 00:31:57,624
a declaration of war.

680
00:31:57,707 --> 00:32:01,628
Think it over, ma'am,
your whole life's on the line.

681
00:32:01,711 --> 00:32:04,714
Why are you so worried
about my life?

682
00:32:08,843 --> 00:32:09,969
Did you just laugh?

683
00:32:10,052 --> 00:32:12,388
It's absurd.

684
00:32:12,471 --> 00:32:15,475
An innocent man could be rotting
behind bars right now,

685
00:32:15,558 --> 00:32:17,477
why are we even
talking about this?

686
00:32:17,560 --> 00:32:18,478
Shut the hell up!

687
00:32:18,561 --> 00:32:21,439
Just think about the victim
who was brutally murdered.

688
00:32:21,522 --> 00:32:23,483
At the very least,

689
00:32:23,566 --> 00:32:26,277
shouldn't we make sure
the real killer is found?

690
00:32:26,360 --> 00:32:29,030
Sgt. Seo, what do you think?

691
00:32:29,572 --> 00:32:30,990
Uh, I think...

692
00:32:31,073 --> 00:32:33,118
since the appeal takes
about a week to start

693
00:32:33,201 --> 00:32:35,662
and the forensics will take
about a week too,

694
00:32:35,745 --> 00:32:37,789
so we work the case for a week

695
00:32:37,872 --> 00:32:39,958
and if anything new
turns up by then,

696
00:32:40,041 --> 00:32:40,750
we go!

697
00:32:40,833 --> 00:32:42,210
If not, stop!

698
00:32:43,502 --> 00:32:44,670
Isn't that fair?

699
00:32:45,504 --> 00:32:47,257
So you're saying you'll do it?

700
00:32:47,340 --> 00:32:51,052
Watch your mouth, chief
and prosecutor are right here!

701
00:32:51,135 --> 00:32:51,553
Excuse me.

702
00:32:51,636 --> 00:32:53,679
What the hell is this guy
even saying right now?

703
00:32:54,639 --> 00:32:55,181
Excuse me!

704
00:32:55,264 --> 00:32:57,058
I'm just trying to
mediate things rationally...

705
00:32:57,934 --> 00:32:59,018
Excuse me!

706
00:33:03,314 --> 00:33:06,150
Let's proceed,
I'll take responsibility.

707
00:33:09,987 --> 00:33:12,740
I'll handle whatever's left
of my life on my own.

708
00:33:18,287 --> 00:33:19,289
Ow!

709
00:33:19,372 --> 00:33:20,415
Ow...

710
00:33:20,498 --> 00:33:23,251
Get up, up you go.

711
00:33:24,252 --> 00:33:25,503
You like playing games?

712
00:33:25,586 --> 00:33:26,671
Yes.

713
00:33:26,754 --> 00:33:27,338
I mean, no!

714
00:33:27,421 --> 00:33:31,884
Go if you find evidence,
stop if you don't?

715
00:33:32,551 --> 00:33:33,803
Is this all a game to you?

716
00:33:33,886 --> 00:33:35,054
Still, sir,

717
00:33:35,554 --> 00:33:37,723
wouldn't it look good
on your record?

718
00:33:38,307 --> 00:33:39,976
How long are you planning to
stay stuck here?

719
00:33:40,059 --> 00:33:41,936
Shouldn't you be climbing
the ladder up at HQ by now?

720
00:33:42,018 --> 00:33:44,855
Like hell I'll get a whiff of
the HQ with you around.

721
00:33:46,691 --> 00:33:48,609
And look at this.

722
00:33:49,151 --> 00:33:50,320
Look at it.

723
00:33:50,403 --> 00:33:52,071
I almost fainted
when I saw it.

724
00:33:52,154 --> 00:33:53,698
What are we gonna do
about this guy?

725
00:33:54,323 --> 00:33:57,076
You saw him earlier,
barking back at me like that.

726
00:33:57,159 --> 00:33:59,704
Yeah, he's a prick,
but at least he's got a spine.

727
00:33:59,787 --> 00:34:00,622
What'd you just say?

728
00:34:00,705 --> 00:34:02,832
You said you'd put
your neck on the line, no?

729
00:34:02,915 --> 00:34:04,167
You know I've got
a heart condition.

730
00:34:04,250 --> 00:34:06,920
You want me to drop dead
five years before retirement?

731
00:34:07,003 --> 00:34:08,337
You want another, punk?

732
00:34:08,838 --> 00:34:09,839
Wait a minute...

733
00:34:09,922 --> 00:34:12,133
I think my shin bone's messed up.

734
00:34:12,216 --> 00:34:13,676
On your feet.

735
00:34:15,386 --> 00:34:18,264
You get demoted again,
that's on you.

736
00:34:18,346 --> 00:34:21,392
Yes, chief! Sgt. Seo Jae-hyuk
reporting for duty!

737
00:34:21,475 --> 00:34:22,476
On assignment!

738
00:34:23,561 --> 00:34:24,645
Son of a...

739
00:34:25,271 --> 00:34:26,272
Get some rest, sir!

740
00:34:39,368 --> 00:34:41,412
What the hell is everyone
doing here?

741
00:34:42,246 --> 00:34:44,082
Can't even close
a single damn case!

742
00:34:44,165 --> 00:34:45,416
By the way, Capt. Oh.

743
00:34:45,499 --> 00:34:47,418
We've got a major case
in our district-

744
00:34:47,500 --> 00:34:48,253
Good afternoon!

745
00:34:48,336 --> 00:34:51,839
Sgt. Seo Jae-hyuk from Boeun PD,
accompanied by one officer.

746
00:34:51,922 --> 00:34:54,175
We're here to formally request

747
00:34:54,258 --> 00:34:56,219
a joint investigation
with Gangnam PD!

748
00:34:56,302 --> 00:34:57,720
Salute!

749
00:35:06,645 --> 00:35:08,314
(Community Sports Room)

750
00:35:08,397 --> 00:35:10,066
(Temporary Joint Investigation HQ)

751
00:35:17,489 --> 00:35:18,532
Everything ready?

752
00:35:20,326 --> 00:35:21,369
Leave.

753
00:35:24,121 --> 00:35:25,415
This is it?

754
00:35:25,498 --> 00:35:26,665
Yeah.

755
00:35:27,666 --> 00:35:29,460
You expect us to work here?

756
00:35:29,543 --> 00:35:31,379
Yeah, if you need anything,

757
00:35:31,462 --> 00:35:32,797
file a request
with the admin office

758
00:35:32,880 --> 00:35:34,299
through official channels.

759
00:35:34,382 --> 00:35:36,175
And the legal cooperation

760
00:35:36,258 --> 00:35:38,094
goes through
the Ministry of Justice.

761
00:35:38,177 --> 00:35:39,887
Are you really going to
act like this?

762
00:35:39,970 --> 00:35:40,638
Yeah.

763
00:35:40,721 --> 00:35:42,556
Plan to do so.

764
00:35:43,974 --> 00:35:45,893
What the hell are you
rummaging through, punk?

765
00:35:45,976 --> 00:35:47,770
Does the internet work here, bud?

766
00:35:47,853 --> 00:35:49,605
Watch your tongue,
you little punk.

767
00:35:49,688 --> 00:35:51,316
Whatever.

768
00:35:51,399 --> 00:35:53,651
Budget's tight, what can I say.

769
00:35:53,734 --> 00:35:57,363
Guys, this is an office now,
play ping-pong quietly.

770
00:35:59,073 --> 00:36:01,617
Use your phone
in this modern age.

771
00:36:10,875 --> 00:36:12,086
Don't take selfies.

772
00:36:12,169 --> 00:36:12,754
Okay.

773
00:36:12,837 --> 00:36:14,380
Run through his profile again.

774
00:36:19,718 --> 00:36:23,348
Cho Dong-oh, 37,
born in Gwangju.

775
00:36:23,431 --> 00:36:25,683
A community college grad,
joined Toyoung Construction.

776
00:36:25,766 --> 00:36:26,559
Quit after a year.

777
00:36:26,642 --> 00:36:29,729
Jumped between companies,
usually quit right away.

778
00:36:29,812 --> 00:36:32,357
Started a loan firm,
ReHigh Capital, four years back.

779
00:36:32,440 --> 00:36:35,276
Married, one daughter.

780
00:36:35,359 --> 00:36:36,069
Why'd you memorize all that?

781
00:36:36,152 --> 00:36:37,320
It's basic prep.

782
00:36:37,403 --> 00:36:38,821
Not really.

783
00:36:39,613 --> 00:36:41,239
He pled not guilty at trial?

784
00:36:41,323 --> 00:36:41,824
Yes.

785
00:36:41,907 --> 00:36:45,536
He confessed during questioning,
then took it back in court.

786
00:36:45,619 --> 00:36:47,913
Why do you think he did that?

787
00:36:49,248 --> 00:36:51,250
You're from the police?

788
00:36:51,333 --> 00:36:52,250
Yes.

789
00:36:53,919 --> 00:36:55,754
We're from Boeun Police Station.

790
00:36:56,422 --> 00:36:58,800
We came to verify a few details
for the investigation.

791
00:36:58,883 --> 00:36:59,884
Mr. Cho,

792
00:36:59,967 --> 00:37:03,346
we caught
a theft suspect recently,

793
00:37:03,429 --> 00:37:04,471
turns out, that guy-

794
00:37:04,555 --> 00:37:06,557
You caught the real killer?

795
00:37:06,640 --> 00:37:07,600
You got him?

796
00:37:07,683 --> 00:37:08,518
Who is it?

797
00:37:08,601 --> 00:37:09,936
That son of a gun!

798
00:37:10,018 --> 00:37:11,979
- I told you I didn't do it!
- Mr. Cho Dong-oh!

799
00:37:12,062 --> 00:37:13,855
I rotted in here for a year
because of this!

800
00:37:13,939 --> 00:37:15,108
- Mr. Cho Dong-oh!
- I'm innocent!

801
00:37:15,191 --> 00:37:17,235
Nothing's been proven yet,
please calm down.

802
00:37:17,317 --> 00:37:18,778
Lee Jin-kyung!

803
00:37:18,861 --> 00:37:21,406
She's lying!
She made it all up!

804
00:37:21,489 --> 00:37:22,824
Alright, okay.

805
00:37:22,907 --> 00:37:25,993
Then tell us, in detail,

806
00:37:26,076 --> 00:37:28,371
what happened that night.

807
00:37:28,454 --> 00:37:30,163
Yes, I'll tell you.

808
00:37:30,247 --> 00:37:32,959
That night,
after a company dinner,

809
00:37:33,042 --> 00:37:34,000
I went to see Min-a.

810
00:37:34,084 --> 00:37:35,586
Why'd you go see her?

811
00:37:35,669 --> 00:37:37,630
Because she and I were
seeing each other!

812
00:37:37,713 --> 00:37:40,424
It was our anniversary,
so I went to give her a gift.

813
00:37:41,383 --> 00:37:42,968
Wow, it looks beautiful.

814
00:37:44,345 --> 00:37:45,513
It really is.

815
00:37:49,892 --> 00:37:52,061
Jin-kyung hated that
we were dating.

816
00:37:52,143 --> 00:37:53,646
And I get it.

817
00:37:53,729 --> 00:37:54,814
It was my fault.

818
00:37:54,897 --> 00:37:57,483
Why didn't Lee Jin-kyung
want you two to meet?

819
00:37:57,566 --> 00:38:00,278
Because... I'm married!

820
00:38:00,361 --> 00:38:00,903
Right.

821
00:38:00,986 --> 00:38:03,864
Yeah, I know, I'm a bad guy.

822
00:38:03,948 --> 00:38:07,076
So you met Min-a,
what happened next?

823
00:38:07,159 --> 00:38:09,787
I drank too much, so I went home
and just passed out.

824
00:38:09,870 --> 00:38:13,458
Next thing I know, cops bust in
and drag me out.

825
00:38:13,541 --> 00:38:14,375
That's everything.

826
00:38:14,458 --> 00:38:17,670
Then why did you confess
to killing her?

827
00:38:17,753 --> 00:38:20,506
They grilled me for three days,

828
00:38:20,589 --> 00:38:23,301
made me repeat myself
a hundred of times.

829
00:38:23,384 --> 00:38:27,054
Later, they said they'd go
find my kid at school.

830
00:38:27,137 --> 00:38:28,389
Who did?

831
00:38:28,471 --> 00:38:29,807
Det. Oh Min-ho.

832
00:38:30,891 --> 00:38:33,602
From Gangnam Police.

833
00:38:34,143 --> 00:38:35,813
Think about it, sergeants,

834
00:38:35,896 --> 00:38:39,984
if a cop shows up
at my eight-year-old's school

835
00:38:40,067 --> 00:38:45,448
and rumor goes around saying
her dad's a murderer...

836
00:38:45,531 --> 00:38:48,409
How is she supposed to
live with that?

837
00:38:48,492 --> 00:38:50,995
Oh Min-ho that jerk is
a real piece of crap!

838
00:38:51,078 --> 00:38:56,125
I cheated on my wife, but murder?
You think I could kill someone?

839
00:38:57,375 --> 00:38:59,962
I didn't kill Min-a! Please!

840
00:39:00,713 --> 00:39:02,256
I'm innocent!

841
00:39:02,339 --> 00:39:04,842
I didn't do it!

842
00:39:07,261 --> 00:39:09,471
(Courthouse)

843
00:39:09,555 --> 00:39:11,098
I'm busy, what's this about?

844
00:39:11,181 --> 00:39:13,392
Sir, there's a problem
with the Lee Min-a case.

845
00:39:13,475 --> 00:39:14,685
What did you just say?

846
00:39:20,149 --> 00:39:21,650
Unbelievable...

847
00:39:22,484 --> 00:39:23,986
What the hell happened?

848
00:39:24,612 --> 00:39:27,406
A thief was arrested in Boeun,

849
00:39:27,489 --> 00:39:31,536
something came up during
questioning that ties to our case.

850
00:39:31,619 --> 00:39:33,287
Right before the appeal trial?

851
00:39:33,370 --> 00:39:35,623
I'll handle the Boeun cops,

852
00:39:35,706 --> 00:39:37,917
just keep their prosecutor
off our backs.

853
00:39:38,000 --> 00:39:40,669
How the hell am I
supposed to do that?

854
00:39:44,214 --> 00:39:46,425
Whatever it takes.

855
00:39:46,508 --> 00:39:51,346
Sir, we're all in this together.

856
00:39:53,098 --> 00:39:54,975
(Cheongju District
Prosecutors' Office)

857
00:39:57,603 --> 00:39:58,813
Prosecutor Kang!

858
00:39:58,896 --> 00:40:02,483
This is Prosecutor Yang
from the Seoul Central District.

859
00:40:02,566 --> 00:40:04,234
My junior from school.

860
00:40:05,903 --> 00:40:07,696
I'm Yang Min-su.

861
00:40:08,864 --> 00:40:10,449
Kang Mi-ju, sir.

862
00:40:13,535 --> 00:40:14,787
Look at her.

863
00:40:16,121 --> 00:40:17,748
Keep on sleeping.

864
00:40:22,294 --> 00:40:24,922
Sorry, sir!

865
00:40:25,631 --> 00:40:27,174
I can't hold my liquor.

866
00:40:29,343 --> 00:40:32,555
Anyway, the Lee Min-a case
is still under our jurisdiction.

867
00:40:32,638 --> 00:40:37,935
If you're reopening it,
you must report to me.

868
00:40:38,018 --> 00:40:39,061
Sir!

869
00:40:39,143 --> 00:40:44,358
I'm not investigating that case.
I'm working on Kang Chang-su's.

870
00:40:45,275 --> 00:40:49,655
He got out last year,
and since then...

871
00:40:50,364 --> 00:40:53,034
The indictment's
already overflowing.

872
00:40:53,117 --> 00:40:54,576
You went to college
in Jeonju, right?

873
00:40:54,660 --> 00:40:55,578
Yes!

874
00:40:55,661 --> 00:40:57,162
Sure.

875
00:40:57,705 --> 00:41:01,584
You've given up on
climbing the ladder,

876
00:41:01,667 --> 00:41:03,961
so you're chasing a big case

877
00:41:04,044 --> 00:41:06,463
to make headlines
before you go private?

878
00:41:08,382 --> 00:41:10,426
That's so tacky.

879
00:41:10,926 --> 00:41:15,180
My dream is to become
the Prosecutor General.

880
00:41:16,181 --> 00:41:17,266
Then I'll help you.

881
00:41:18,308 --> 00:41:20,643
I said I'll put you forward.

882
00:41:21,603 --> 00:41:25,191
You've got no connections,
no one will be watching you.

883
00:41:25,274 --> 00:41:27,692
I could have you assigned to

884
00:41:27,776 --> 00:41:30,154
Seoul's Special Investigations
next month.

885
00:41:31,864 --> 00:41:33,657
Sir, do you...

886
00:41:36,951 --> 00:41:38,454
like me?

887
00:41:39,830 --> 00:41:40,663
What?

888
00:41:42,374 --> 00:41:46,003
I'm sorry, but I can't
return those feelings.

889
00:41:46,086 --> 00:41:47,046
Are you kidding me?

890
00:41:47,129 --> 00:41:48,547
I'm sorry, sir...

891
00:41:49,214 --> 00:41:50,632
Thank you for the drink.

892
00:41:52,468 --> 00:41:54,011
No, no, Kang, no way!

893
00:41:54,094 --> 00:41:54,970
I don't like you.

894
00:41:55,053 --> 00:41:55,805
Goodbye, sir.

895
00:41:55,888 --> 00:41:57,098
I said I don't like you!

896
00:41:57,181 --> 00:42:00,685
I like you? Wait a minute!

897
00:42:00,768 --> 00:42:01,893
Kang!

898
00:42:01,977 --> 00:42:03,812
The problem is

899
00:42:04,730 --> 00:42:10,611
why won't people just
leave people like me alone?

900
00:42:13,530 --> 00:42:15,991
Do you understand
where I'm coming from?

901
00:42:16,825 --> 00:42:20,621
I'm really sorry, ma'am,
but may I hang up now?

902
00:42:22,288 --> 00:42:26,252
I worked my butt off

903
00:42:26,335 --> 00:42:30,005
to become a prosecutor
because of you!

904
00:42:30,088 --> 00:42:32,717
I can't hear you, ma'am.
I need to hang up now.

905
00:42:32,800 --> 00:42:34,384
Hello?

906
00:42:36,345 --> 00:42:37,763
Did you hang up?

907
00:42:38,971 --> 00:42:40,224
Hello?

908
00:42:42,976 --> 00:42:45,020
Who were you talking to
at this hour?

909
00:42:46,355 --> 00:42:48,315
Do I have to report
my personal calls now?

910
00:42:48,398 --> 00:42:50,359
If it's getting in the way,
maybe you should quit!

911
00:42:50,442 --> 00:42:51,276
Sure.

912
00:42:51,777 --> 00:42:53,320
Did you find anything?

913
00:42:55,280 --> 00:42:56,614
Did you buy these yourself?

914
00:42:57,114 --> 00:42:58,451
I brought them from home.

915
00:42:58,534 --> 00:42:59,660
But...

916
00:43:00,369 --> 00:43:02,913
all the important stuff
has been redacted.

917
00:43:02,996 --> 00:43:04,874
They sure did because

918
00:43:04,957 --> 00:43:06,834
they got no intention
of cooperating.

919
00:43:06,917 --> 00:43:09,002
We need to dig
everything up ourselves.

920
00:43:11,046 --> 00:43:12,965
(Room 2104)

921
00:43:13,047 --> 00:43:14,550
According to the statement,

922
00:43:14,633 --> 00:43:16,343
you saw your sister
with Cho Dong-oh

923
00:43:16,426 --> 00:43:18,137
on the night of the incident.

924
00:43:18,220 --> 00:43:20,848
What time was it exactly?

925
00:43:20,931 --> 00:43:22,725
It's written there.

926
00:43:22,808 --> 00:43:26,854
I know it's hard to relive this,
but we need you to be precise.

927
00:43:26,937 --> 00:43:28,147
A wrongly convicted man

928
00:43:28,230 --> 00:43:29,398
might be sitting in
a cell right now.

929
00:43:30,023 --> 00:43:34,027
My sister worked herself to death
to pay for my tuition,

930
00:43:34,570 --> 00:43:36,947
my dad's hospital bills,
and food for our family.

931
00:43:37,030 --> 00:43:40,367
Then a year ago,
she came back as a cold corpse.

932
00:43:41,535 --> 00:43:43,537
You tell me, sergeant.

933
00:43:43,620 --> 00:43:45,663
Who do you think feels wronged?

934
00:43:57,801 --> 00:43:59,678
What are you doing, sir?

935
00:43:59,761 --> 00:44:01,763
Go keep watch outside.

936
00:44:02,681 --> 00:44:04,433
You learned stuff from a book,

937
00:44:04,516 --> 00:44:06,101
you don't know anything
about real field work.

938
00:44:06,184 --> 00:44:08,103
Isn't that illegal?

939
00:44:08,186 --> 00:44:11,023
You're worried about that now?
What about perjury?

940
00:44:11,105 --> 00:44:12,525
Who's the real perp?

941
00:44:12,608 --> 00:44:13,192
Kang Chang-su.

942
00:44:13,275 --> 00:44:16,987
But she testified that
it was Cho Dong-oh.

943
00:44:17,070 --> 00:44:18,864
Isn't that strange?

944
00:44:20,157 --> 00:44:21,325
It is.

945
00:44:29,416 --> 00:44:30,792
Very strange.

946
00:44:33,462 --> 00:44:34,839
What's so strange about it?

947
00:44:34,922 --> 00:44:38,676
Kang was carrying
the same talisman.

948
00:44:38,759 --> 00:44:40,802
Min-a's keepsake,
that's solid evidence.

949
00:44:41,637 --> 00:44:43,596
Why would sisters carry
matching talismans?

950
00:44:43,680 --> 00:44:44,681
Go away!

951
00:44:45,265 --> 00:44:47,601
Maybe it's some kind of
lucky charm?

952
00:44:47,684 --> 00:44:50,187
Lucky charm?
What the hell do you know?

953
00:44:50,270 --> 00:44:53,148
You've only studied
police work in textbooks.

954
00:45:02,074 --> 00:45:04,618
I'm so tired!

955
00:45:07,788 --> 00:45:09,665
I'm doing all the leg work,

956
00:45:09,748 --> 00:45:13,460
while my partner just hunches over
a computer all day.

957
00:45:13,543 --> 00:45:14,461
Come take a look.

958
00:45:14,544 --> 00:45:15,254
What?

959
00:45:15,337 --> 00:45:17,422
I think I got a match.

960
00:45:21,093 --> 00:45:22,845
“Taegang Fortune Hall”?

961
00:45:22,928 --> 00:45:25,264
How did you find this?

962
00:45:25,346 --> 00:45:27,600
You didn't learn police work
from a textbook,

963
00:45:27,683 --> 00:45:29,726
so you're clueless.

964
00:45:31,728 --> 00:45:32,980
High-five!

965
00:45:34,398 --> 00:45:36,025
Let's see...

966
00:45:36,108 --> 00:45:39,569
So, it was May, 2018...

967
00:45:40,320 --> 00:45:44,074
Here, it says she bought it.

968
00:45:44,157 --> 00:45:45,409
Is that so?

969
00:45:47,076 --> 00:45:49,663
It's popular among young women.

970
00:45:50,288 --> 00:45:51,081
It's called...

971
00:45:51,163 --> 00:45:55,711
a ‘stalker talisman, '
it's quite potent.

972
00:45:55,794 --> 00:45:59,464
Does this talisman look different
from other fortunetellers?

973
00:46:01,133 --> 00:46:02,092
Of course.

974
00:46:02,926 --> 00:46:05,721
I only sell my own talismans.

975
00:46:07,264 --> 00:46:08,432
Wait a sec...

976
00:46:09,349 --> 00:46:12,477
It says the sisters took
two identical talismans.

977
00:46:13,186 --> 00:46:14,146
Why would they do that?

978
00:46:14,229 --> 00:46:19,484
Can you make me
the exact same one?

979
00:46:23,780 --> 00:46:26,742
You can skip the blessing part.
Just make it the same.

980
00:46:26,825 --> 00:46:27,617
Out.

981
00:46:28,201 --> 00:46:29,453
Out!

982
00:46:29,536 --> 00:46:30,746
Come on...

983
00:46:30,829 --> 00:46:31,705
Got any money?

984
00:46:32,581 --> 00:46:33,374
Do you take cards?

985
00:46:33,457 --> 00:46:35,208
Buddy, a credit card here?

986
00:46:37,335 --> 00:46:39,504
VAT is extra.

987
00:46:43,550 --> 00:46:44,468
Still haven't found it?

988
00:46:44,551 --> 00:46:46,887
I'm looking for it!

989
00:46:50,557 --> 00:46:52,643
Put some real effort
into finding it.

990
00:46:52,726 --> 00:46:54,518
Yeah, hold on.

991
00:47:21,129 --> 00:47:21,880
Ma'am.

992
00:47:21,963 --> 00:47:24,466
This proves that Kang
is the perp, right?

993
00:47:24,549 --> 00:47:28,637
You think a judge will convict him
with this kind of evidence?

994
00:47:29,221 --> 00:47:30,931
It's still circumstantial.

995
00:47:31,014 --> 00:47:32,808
To indict we need firmer proof.

996
00:47:32,891 --> 00:47:34,977
And the hammer from Kang's car?

997
00:47:35,060 --> 00:47:37,062
The forensic results should
be out by tomorrow.

998
00:47:37,145 --> 00:47:38,438
By the way...

999
00:47:39,898 --> 00:47:42,109
why are we having a meeting here?

1000
00:47:42,192 --> 00:47:42,860
That's because...

1001
00:47:42,942 --> 00:47:44,528
Your food is here.

1002
00:47:46,947 --> 00:47:50,075
I just wanted to check on
my kid before I leave.

1003
00:47:50,158 --> 00:47:51,701
I want to see her while I'm here.

1004
00:47:53,120 --> 00:47:54,079
How old is she?

1005
00:47:54,162 --> 00:47:57,041
Why do you want to know that?
With a grin no less.

1006
00:47:57,124 --> 00:47:57,916
You're so creepy.

1007
00:47:57,999 --> 00:47:59,500
What? I was just asking.

1008
00:47:59,584 --> 00:48:00,919
So why are you asking?

1009
00:48:01,002 --> 00:48:02,671
It's so creepy to ask that
with that grin.

1010
00:48:02,754 --> 00:48:05,297
- Stop saying creepy.
- Why do you...

1011
00:48:06,341 --> 00:48:07,509
Dad!

1012
00:48:09,344 --> 00:48:10,220
Careful!

1013
00:48:12,806 --> 00:48:14,933
In the back, come on out!

1014
00:48:15,725 --> 00:48:17,643
How old are you?

1015
00:48:17,727 --> 00:48:19,772
We'll confirm, sir.

1016
00:48:19,855 --> 00:48:21,105
Go standby outside.

1017
00:48:21,773 --> 00:48:24,860
You're chasing customers away
during peak hours,

1018
00:48:24,942 --> 00:48:26,570
what are you up to?

1019
00:48:27,070 --> 00:48:29,781
Why didn't you report this
as an entertainment establishment?

1020
00:48:31,241 --> 00:48:32,785
You know what happens

1021
00:48:32,868 --> 00:48:34,451
if a regular diner
runs hostess services.

1022
00:48:35,203 --> 00:48:36,997
What do you want from me?

1023
00:48:46,631 --> 00:48:47,800
Yes, Kim Joong-ho speaking.

1024
00:48:47,883 --> 00:48:50,636
Sgt. Hottie, it's Lee Hwa-ran.

1025
00:48:50,719 --> 00:48:51,845
Pardon? Who?

1026
00:48:51,928 --> 00:48:54,640
You came by before,

1027
00:48:54,723 --> 00:48:55,682
The Nest.

1028
00:48:55,765 --> 00:48:58,351
Yes, what can I do for you?

1029
00:49:08,236 --> 00:49:10,197
Why are you poking around
the victim's family?

1030
00:49:10,280 --> 00:49:12,241
What's wrong with interviewing
the victim's circle?

1031
00:49:12,324 --> 00:49:15,953
And you get paid our taxes
so you should work

1032
00:49:16,036 --> 00:49:17,871
instead of following us around.

1033
00:49:19,456 --> 00:49:20,415
So?

1034
00:49:21,166 --> 00:49:22,209
How's the investigation going?

1035
00:49:22,292 --> 00:49:23,544
The case's going nowhere,

1036
00:49:23,627 --> 00:49:24,962
but my ping pong drive
is getting better.

1037
00:49:25,045 --> 00:49:27,255
It's getting precise.

1038
00:49:29,007 --> 00:49:30,717
I talked to Baek Dae-hoon.

1039
00:49:30,800 --> 00:49:33,094
Apparently, you didn't leave
much of an impression.

1040
00:49:33,595 --> 00:49:35,139
He said he vaguely remembers

1041
00:49:35,221 --> 00:49:38,267
a flimsy guy who got into a mess
and exiled out to the countryside.

1042
00:49:38,350 --> 00:49:42,145
People were apparently ecstatic
when you were kicked out.

1043
00:49:43,480 --> 00:49:44,439
So?

1044
00:49:45,523 --> 00:49:50,863
You scared that some village cops
will expose a wrongful arrest?

1045
00:49:50,946 --> 00:49:54,199
Bored of cleaning up punk trash
in the countryside?

1046
00:49:54,282 --> 00:49:56,201
So you keep poking around Seoul?

1047
00:49:56,785 --> 00:50:01,163
Drop this and head back,
you country bumpkin.

1048
00:50:01,748 --> 00:50:03,875
Cho Dong-oh is the perp.

1049
00:50:03,959 --> 00:50:06,712
He's not a perp,
he's a suspect to me!

1050
00:50:06,795 --> 00:50:07,754
A suspect?

1051
00:50:09,756 --> 00:50:13,009
Even if there's mountains of
evidence and witnesses?

1052
00:50:14,928 --> 00:50:16,638
Work hard, bud.

1053
00:50:16,721 --> 00:50:19,391
Eat up, you'll need the strength.

1054
00:50:20,976 --> 00:50:22,936
Oh, by the way...

1055
00:50:24,854 --> 00:50:26,230
watch your back.

1056
00:50:27,357 --> 00:50:29,401
I play dirty.

1057
00:50:31,403 --> 00:50:32,487
Idiot...

1058
00:50:51,589 --> 00:50:53,217
Can you wake up?

1059
00:50:53,300 --> 00:50:53,842
Madame!

1060
00:50:53,925 --> 00:50:55,343
You jerk!

1061
00:50:56,386 --> 00:50:56,929
Sir.

1062
00:50:57,012 --> 00:50:58,513
- Are you nuts?
- Pardon?

1063
00:51:00,056 --> 00:51:00,641
Madame?

1064
00:51:00,724 --> 00:51:01,933
You little crap!

1065
00:51:02,642 --> 00:51:03,435
What the hell are you doing?

1066
00:51:03,518 --> 00:51:04,186
What's with you?

1067
00:51:04,268 --> 00:51:06,104
What have you done?

1068
00:51:07,480 --> 00:51:08,690
It's not what you think.

1069
00:51:08,773 --> 00:51:10,025
Not what I think?

1070
00:51:10,108 --> 00:51:11,942
Just listen for a second.

1071
00:51:12,569 --> 00:51:14,363
This is the IOU
Min-a took from me

1072
00:51:14,446 --> 00:51:16,156
to pay her father's
hospital bills.

1073
00:51:16,239 --> 00:51:17,950
Why show me this?

1074
00:51:18,033 --> 00:51:21,828
Last time those sergeants
told us not to hand it over

1075
00:51:21,911 --> 00:51:23,872
and said this evidence
might helps Cho.

1076
00:51:24,538 --> 00:51:26,082
Shall we drink?

1077
00:51:29,210 --> 00:51:30,003
Cheers.

1078
00:51:34,215 --> 00:51:35,926
Why is this lady passed out?

1079
00:51:36,009 --> 00:51:39,137
Something felt off,
so I swapped the drinks,

1080
00:51:39,220 --> 00:51:40,305
and she passed out.

1081
00:51:40,388 --> 00:51:41,890
She was trying to
slip you something?

1082
00:51:41,973 --> 00:51:42,724
Right.

1083
00:51:42,807 --> 00:51:45,393
Those Gangnam jerks
are pulling her strings!

1084
00:51:45,477 --> 00:51:49,064
They were trying to
mess with my boy?

1085
00:51:50,357 --> 00:51:51,275
And you!

1086
00:51:51,358 --> 00:51:53,402
Shouldn't you report to me
before the field work?

1087
00:51:53,485 --> 00:51:56,029
You can't just
run off on your own!

1088
00:51:56,112 --> 00:51:57,531
Act first, report later!

1089
00:51:57,614 --> 00:51:58,991
Isn't it
“report first, act later”?

1090
00:51:59,074 --> 00:52:01,785
Who cares about semantics now?

1091
00:52:02,744 --> 00:52:03,996
That's...

1092
00:52:04,079 --> 00:52:06,288
what this lady was
trying to get me to drink.

1093
00:52:08,124 --> 00:52:09,668
She wasn't trying to
slip you booze?

1094
00:52:09,750 --> 00:52:11,795
How could I drink alcohol
while on duty?

1095
00:52:11,878 --> 00:52:15,549
It's just a soft drink.

1096
00:52:15,632 --> 00:52:16,883
So you swapped pops?

1097
00:52:16,966 --> 00:52:17,509
Yes.

1098
00:52:17,592 --> 00:52:19,469
Why didn't you say so?

1099
00:52:19,552 --> 00:52:21,096
Why do you drink random stuff?

1100
00:52:21,179 --> 00:52:23,098
Report first, act later, dammit!

1101
00:52:23,181 --> 00:52:24,850
I was going to report,
but you already drank it!

1102
00:52:24,933 --> 00:52:27,143
You don't report anything!

1103
00:52:27,227 --> 00:52:28,978
You just drink...

1104
00:52:29,604 --> 00:52:30,814
- What's that?
- Sirens?

1105
00:52:36,736 --> 00:52:38,738
Who the hell?
No freaking way!

1106
00:52:39,739 --> 00:52:40,949
It's a trap!

1107
00:52:41,032 --> 00:52:42,951
- Open the shutter!
- Sir!

1108
00:52:43,034 --> 00:52:45,037
Open this gate!

1109
00:52:45,120 --> 00:52:48,038
Let go of me!
We're the police!

1110
00:52:48,915 --> 00:52:50,709
Open this gate!

1111
00:52:50,792 --> 00:52:52,377
Open this gate at once!

1112
00:53:09,978 --> 00:53:11,521
What's up?

1113
00:53:12,230 --> 00:53:13,315
What did you eat?

1114
00:53:13,398 --> 00:53:14,357
What?

1115
00:53:15,650 --> 00:53:16,901
Block him!

1116
00:53:18,069 --> 00:53:19,654
(Narcotics Division)

1117
00:53:19,737 --> 00:53:21,072
It came out negative.

1118
00:53:22,532 --> 00:53:25,118
This is insane.

1119
00:53:26,619 --> 00:53:29,080
- Why didn't it come up?
- They're coming.

1120
00:53:33,625 --> 00:53:34,628
You got lucky.

1121
00:53:34,711 --> 00:53:36,504
No, you're the lucky ones.

1122
00:53:37,172 --> 00:53:39,257
Because I'm way too nice.

1123
00:53:40,049 --> 00:53:43,094
But there's one thing
I never let slide.

1124
00:53:43,636 --> 00:53:44,554
And what's that?

1125
00:53:44,637 --> 00:53:46,346
Messing with my family.

1126
00:53:49,434 --> 00:53:50,768
You son of a...

1127
00:53:50,852 --> 00:53:51,686
Step back!

1128
00:53:52,228 --> 00:53:53,563
Don't touch me, jerk!

1129
00:53:53,646 --> 00:53:56,066
Ever hear of entrapment,
and how it's illegal?

1130
00:53:56,149 --> 00:53:58,442
The way you're going at
fellow cops like this,

1131
00:53:58,526 --> 00:54:00,362
there's something fishy
going on here, right?

1132
00:54:00,445 --> 00:54:03,239
We got a witness testimony,
and physical evidence,

1133
00:54:03,323 --> 00:54:05,867
even DNA evidence too,
so what's the problem?

1134
00:54:05,950 --> 00:54:08,620
The witness had
a grudge against Cho,

1135
00:54:08,703 --> 00:54:10,372
and you guys planted the DNA.

1136
00:54:10,455 --> 00:54:11,790
What did you say?

1137
00:54:11,873 --> 00:54:13,208
Planted?

1138
00:54:13,291 --> 00:54:14,709
Can you prove that?

1139
00:54:14,792 --> 00:54:18,588
What is your obsession
with Cho Dong-oh?

1140
00:54:18,671 --> 00:54:20,507
Because he's the perp.

1141
00:54:20,590 --> 00:54:22,217
I know that prick well.

1142
00:54:22,884 --> 00:54:25,178
He deserves to
rot in prison for life.

1143
00:54:25,261 --> 00:54:27,431
I'll make sure he does.

1144
00:54:27,514 --> 00:54:29,724
Kang Chang-su's the perp.

1145
00:54:30,600 --> 00:54:32,727
I've gotten to know
that jerk real well.

1146
00:54:33,561 --> 00:54:36,898
Cho should walk free,
and Kang should be locked up.

1147
00:54:37,774 --> 00:54:39,901
I'll make sure he does.

1148
00:54:52,747 --> 00:54:54,415
(DUI Check)

1149
00:54:58,753 --> 00:55:01,465
That black BMW's been bugging me.

1150
00:55:01,547 --> 00:55:03,758
It's probably the Gangnam guys.

1151
00:55:04,425 --> 00:55:07,387
Entrapment cops driving
a BMW, what a joke.

1152
00:55:07,470 --> 00:55:09,681
Those are common around here.

1153
00:55:10,431 --> 00:55:12,267
They lease them at premium rates.

1154
00:55:17,689 --> 00:55:18,982
By the way, sir,

1155
00:55:19,482 --> 00:55:21,942
remember the first part
of Kang's testimony?

1156
00:55:22,694 --> 00:55:24,154
What about it?

1157
00:55:24,237 --> 00:55:26,573
I got drunk and took
the wrong cab...

1158
00:55:26,656 --> 00:55:28,617
How he got too drunk
and took the cab.

1159
00:55:28,700 --> 00:55:29,284
And?

1160
00:55:29,367 --> 00:55:31,161
Even if he's drunk,
he had his own car.

1161
00:55:31,244 --> 00:55:33,705
He could've called a temp driver.

1162
00:55:35,081 --> 00:55:38,084
Then maybe he lied in the moment.

1163
00:55:38,668 --> 00:55:39,836
To cover up drunk driving!

1164
00:55:39,919 --> 00:55:40,587
Right!

1165
00:55:40,670 --> 00:55:42,505
So he actually drove himself!

1166
00:55:43,089 --> 00:55:44,799
Hey, turn the car around.

1167
00:55:44,882 --> 00:55:46,634
- Pardon?
- Turn it around now!

1168
00:55:46,718 --> 00:55:48,094
- Where to?
- Gangnam precinct.

1169
00:55:48,177 --> 00:55:50,555
We need to check the CCTV footage.

1170
00:55:50,638 --> 00:55:53,183
Kang's car might show up there.

1171
00:55:53,266 --> 00:55:55,393
But CCTV's only stored
for three months.

1172
00:55:55,476 --> 00:55:59,063
That's for traffic cases,
but three years for criminal ones.

1173
00:56:03,692 --> 00:56:06,279
Wait! Stop! Stop!

1174
00:56:07,905 --> 00:56:09,907
We'll take this one!
We got it!

1175
00:56:12,744 --> 00:56:14,996
Are you seriously stopping
at the red light?

1176
00:56:17,582 --> 00:56:19,125
Should I lose them?

1177
00:56:19,208 --> 00:56:20,210
Can you do it?

1178
00:56:20,293 --> 00:56:24,297
You made an illegal U-turn,
but stop at the re...

1179
00:56:25,047 --> 00:56:26,341
Hold on tight.

1180
00:56:30,261 --> 00:56:31,220
Easy, easy!

1181
00:56:38,561 --> 00:56:40,271
Why is he so good at driving?

1182
00:56:42,398 --> 00:56:43,984
The car's not picking up speed.

1183
00:56:44,067 --> 00:56:46,278
Is that an excuse?
It sure sounds like it.

1184
00:56:46,361 --> 00:56:49,281
If they catch us,
we're both doomed!

1185
00:56:49,364 --> 00:56:51,950
We'll be yanked off the case,
and sent back to the sticks!

1186
00:56:52,033 --> 00:56:53,785
What a jalopy!

1187
00:56:53,868 --> 00:56:54,744
Here we go!

1188
00:56:56,537 --> 00:56:58,206
Stay on them! Over there!

1189
00:57:03,002 --> 00:57:04,671
Okay, let's do this for real.

1190
00:57:04,754 --> 00:57:06,881
Super real, just do it!

1191
00:57:06,964 --> 00:57:08,299
Lose them at all costs!

1192
00:57:11,552 --> 00:57:12,679
Dammit!

1193
00:57:14,180 --> 00:57:15,932
Where are they going?

1194
00:57:21,354 --> 00:57:22,772
It's no time to celebrate.

1195
00:57:22,855 --> 00:57:23,773
You laugh?

1196
00:57:25,983 --> 00:57:27,735
Look at these jerks.

1197
00:57:34,826 --> 00:57:36,161
Where are you going?

1198
00:57:36,244 --> 00:57:37,120
Home.

1199
00:57:37,912 --> 00:57:39,038
Your home?

1200
00:57:39,956 --> 00:57:40,915
Yes.

1201
00:57:57,348 --> 00:57:58,975
What the hell, man!

1202
00:58:01,477 --> 00:58:02,520
Hop in.

1203
00:58:03,938 --> 00:58:05,815
This car sticks out
like a sore thumb.

1204
00:58:05,898 --> 00:58:07,108
Just get in, quick.

1205
00:58:08,568 --> 00:58:10,820
Why's it orange?
It looks like a taxi.

1206
00:58:12,405 --> 00:58:14,699
Did we lose them?

1207
00:58:18,661 --> 00:58:19,663
What's this?

1208
00:58:19,746 --> 00:58:21,081
What do we do?

1209
00:58:21,164 --> 00:58:22,749
Can they see us?

1210
00:58:22,832 --> 00:58:23,667
No.

1211
00:58:23,750 --> 00:58:25,001
What will you do then?

1212
00:58:25,793 --> 00:58:26,920
Just watch.

1213
00:58:27,003 --> 00:58:29,172
I'm in the passenger seat,
what else can I do?

1214
00:58:29,255 --> 00:58:31,215
Hey, hey, easy!

1215
00:58:34,844 --> 00:58:37,138
Even if it's a Lambo,
this is a one-way alley!

1216
00:58:37,221 --> 00:58:38,306
What's with him?

1217
00:58:41,726 --> 00:58:44,061
Damn, where's the handle?

1218
00:58:46,397 --> 00:58:47,648
Back up! Hurry!

1219
00:58:55,865 --> 00:58:57,617
Sorry.

1220
00:58:57,700 --> 00:58:59,494
You're driving like a lunatic!

1221
00:58:59,577 --> 00:59:01,412
I'm sorry, no need to get angry...

1222
00:59:02,205 --> 00:59:03,331
Hold on.

1223
00:59:07,001 --> 00:59:09,003
Keep it up,
clean up properly.

1224
00:59:16,803 --> 00:59:18,888
You're cocky behind the wheel!

1225
00:59:18,971 --> 00:59:19,597
Pardon?

1226
00:59:19,680 --> 00:59:21,558
You were power tripping!

1227
00:59:21,641 --> 00:59:23,434
I've always been cocky, sir.

1228
00:59:43,162 --> 00:59:44,705
You lost them?

1229
00:59:47,416 --> 00:59:49,377
Yeah, you'd better be sorry.

1230
00:59:50,127 --> 00:59:52,213
If you're sorry,
then go find them again!

1231
00:59:52,922 --> 00:59:54,882
What? What about the car?

1232
00:59:56,968 --> 00:59:59,471
That car's rented under my name...

1233
00:59:59,554 --> 01:00:02,098
What happens if we get caught?

1234
01:00:03,182 --> 01:00:06,185
Then you're fired and off to work
for your dad's company.

1235
01:00:07,144 --> 01:00:08,396
What about you, sir?

1236
01:00:08,479 --> 01:00:09,105
Me?

1237
01:00:09,188 --> 01:00:10,648
Get me a job at his company too.

1238
01:00:10,731 --> 01:00:12,734
Come on, that's embarrassing.

1239
01:00:12,817 --> 01:00:14,903
I'm not going to starve.

1240
01:00:14,986 --> 01:00:19,657
Why were those jerks trying
so damn hard to shake us off?

1241
01:00:20,366 --> 01:00:21,576
Indeed, Captain.

1242
01:00:21,659 --> 01:00:23,536
Is that all you know how to say?

1243
01:00:30,668 --> 01:00:31,627
Yo, bro!

1244
01:00:33,087 --> 01:00:35,173
Police station!

1245
01:00:35,256 --> 01:00:37,341
I got busted for a DUI, yo!

1246
01:00:38,217 --> 01:00:41,178
Only had a sip, and these
Seoul cops dragged me in.

1247
01:00:45,016 --> 01:00:47,476
I'm taking a drunken poop.

1248
01:00:48,811 --> 01:00:50,187
Call you later.

1249
01:00:53,107 --> 01:00:55,151
That BMW repair's going to
cost a fortune.

1250
01:00:55,234 --> 01:00:58,571
Christ, you sure
can't read the room...

1251
01:00:59,280 --> 01:01:00,156
Hey.

1252
01:01:00,740 --> 01:01:02,075
Yes, sir?

1253
01:01:02,158 --> 01:01:04,536
Why'd a DUIer come down here
to take a dump?

1254
01:01:04,619 --> 01:01:05,661
Indeed, Captain.

1255
01:01:07,914 --> 01:01:09,957
Those sons of guns...

1256
01:01:18,341 --> 01:01:19,675
Look at these punks.

1257
01:01:25,431 --> 01:01:26,223
What's up?

1258
01:01:26,807 --> 01:01:27,934
Just felt like it.

1259
01:01:28,017 --> 01:01:29,226
Dammit...

1260
01:01:32,605 --> 01:01:34,190
This is so frustrating.

1261
01:01:34,273 --> 01:01:36,526
Did you check the camera IDs
near The Nest?

1262
01:01:36,609 --> 01:01:39,904
Yes, only one road in and out,
so I just need to enter the times.

1263
01:01:42,740 --> 01:01:43,616
Camera 6.

1264
01:01:44,533 --> 01:01:45,577
Which side is that?

1265
01:01:45,660 --> 01:01:46,786
Looks like the data archive room.

1266
01:01:46,869 --> 01:01:48,704
Those little...

1267
01:01:51,040 --> 01:01:52,375
The blue car...

1268
01:01:54,210 --> 01:01:55,461
Move your butt!

1269
01:01:56,337 --> 01:01:57,672
I got a hit, sir.

1270
01:01:59,048 --> 01:01:59,799
What's the plate number?

1271
01:01:59,882 --> 01:02:01,551
Can't make it out clearly.

1272
01:02:01,634 --> 01:02:04,095
Pull every feed around that time.

1273
01:02:04,178 --> 01:02:05,471
He has to be there.

1274
01:02:10,935 --> 01:02:11,894
Nothing here.

1275
01:02:12,645 --> 01:02:13,605
Same here!

1276
01:02:13,688 --> 01:02:15,940
- Go and find them!
- Yes, Captain.

1277
01:02:16,023 --> 01:02:16,983
Let's move!

1278
01:02:22,488 --> 01:02:24,073
What were you two doing in here?

1279
01:02:25,658 --> 01:02:28,077
As of today,
this joint op is over.

1280
01:02:28,703 --> 01:02:29,996
And from now on,
you're both criminals.

1281
01:02:30,079 --> 01:02:31,539
Press any key on the laptop.

1282
01:02:34,458 --> 01:02:36,294
Blue Sportage,
license plate 5734.

1283
01:02:36,377 --> 01:02:38,379
Registered to Kang Chang-su.

1284
01:02:38,462 --> 01:02:43,009
See him driving into the village
at 10:57 p.m., June 17th?

1285
01:02:43,092 --> 01:02:44,719
Skip to the next frame,

1286
01:02:44,802 --> 01:02:46,763
1:43 a.m., June 18th,

1287
01:02:46,846 --> 01:02:50,766
you'll see the same Sportage
leaving the village.

1288
01:02:51,892 --> 01:02:54,520
I'm sorry for taking the case
files without permission.

1289
01:02:55,312 --> 01:02:57,607
But you guys did us dirty too.

1290
01:02:57,690 --> 01:02:58,608
To be honest,

1291
01:02:58,691 --> 01:03:02,236
I pushed hard
just to beat you.

1292
01:03:02,319 --> 01:03:04,322
But after all this,

1293
01:03:04,405 --> 01:03:06,615
it's not about winning
or losing anymore.

1294
01:03:07,283 --> 01:03:09,702
It's about finding the truth.

1295
01:03:11,370 --> 01:03:13,414
I hope you see that too.

1296
01:03:13,497 --> 01:03:15,708
Because we're
the same kind of cops, right?

1297
01:03:23,174 --> 01:03:24,383
Hello?

1298
01:03:31,223 --> 01:03:32,100
Who is it?

1299
01:03:32,183 --> 01:03:33,559
Police, ma'am.

1300
01:03:33,642 --> 01:03:36,270
Is your husband, Cho Dong-oh?

1301
01:03:36,353 --> 01:03:38,606
Yes, he's in prison,
he's not here.

1302
01:03:38,689 --> 01:03:41,734
We just want to ask
a few questions about him.

1303
01:03:41,817 --> 01:03:42,735
Okay.

1304
01:03:42,818 --> 01:03:45,279
Could you open the door
a little more?

1305
01:03:46,238 --> 01:03:47,114
Okay.

1306
01:03:48,199 --> 01:03:50,034
Thank you, good afternoon.

1307
01:03:50,117 --> 01:03:51,202
Hello.

1308
01:03:51,285 --> 01:03:53,830
The appeal trial's about to start.

1309
01:03:53,913 --> 01:03:54,288
Yes.

1310
01:03:54,371 --> 01:03:56,916
We think there might be
some misinformation.

1311
01:04:00,127 --> 01:04:01,962
- It's Ye-sol.
- Pardon?

1312
01:04:07,802 --> 01:04:09,345
It's all lies.

1313
01:04:10,679 --> 01:04:14,016
Ms. Lee, you're the one
who lied first.

1314
01:04:14,558 --> 01:04:17,186
You do know perjury's
a criminal offense, right?

1315
01:04:17,269 --> 01:04:18,604
Ms. Lee.

1316
01:04:20,648 --> 01:04:23,234
We're on your side.

1317
01:04:23,317 --> 01:04:25,820
For you sister's sake,

1318
01:04:25,903 --> 01:04:27,905
please tell us the truth.

1319
01:04:30,157 --> 01:04:31,576
Did you get hurt?

1320
01:04:31,659 --> 01:04:32,535
Yes.

1321
01:04:33,744 --> 01:04:35,038
What happened?

1322
01:04:35,121 --> 01:04:37,998
My... my husband.

1323
01:04:39,083 --> 01:04:40,292
Your husband?

1324
01:04:41,377 --> 01:04:44,046
When he gets angry,
he slashes me.

1325
01:04:46,799 --> 01:04:49,051
About two months
before my sister died,

1326
01:04:52,304 --> 01:04:54,390
he came to the hospital.

1327
01:04:55,349 --> 01:04:59,353
He had a $30,000 promissory note.

1328
01:04:59,854 --> 01:05:04,275
He said she borrowed money
for our father's treatment.

1329
01:05:04,942 --> 01:05:08,446
Then he told me
I had to pay it back.

1330
01:05:08,529 --> 01:05:12,241
He said he'd sue her otherwise.

1331
01:05:12,324 --> 01:05:15,244
But I didn't have the money.

1332
01:05:20,166 --> 01:05:22,793
After that,
he kept calling me out.

1333
01:05:23,752 --> 01:05:29,258
Even the night my sister died,
I got his call.

1334
01:05:30,050 --> 01:05:32,595
Why didn't you report him?

1335
01:05:34,138 --> 01:05:35,973
I can't report...

1336
01:05:36,765 --> 01:05:38,017
What?

1337
01:05:38,100 --> 01:05:39,685
He said if I did,

1338
01:05:41,729 --> 01:05:46,358
he'd take Ye-sol away from me.

1339
01:05:48,694 --> 01:05:49,821
I'm sorry...

1340
01:05:49,904 --> 01:05:52,240
I'm so sorry,
I'm sorry!

1341
01:05:52,323 --> 01:05:53,908
I'm so sorry!

1342
01:05:53,991 --> 01:05:57,203
I just want to live with Ye-sol,

1343
01:05:57,286 --> 01:05:58,704
I'm sorry!

1344
01:06:01,874 --> 01:06:03,126
He's a monster!

1345
01:06:03,209 --> 01:06:05,795
You perjured yourself
out of hatred for Cho Dong-oh!

1346
01:06:05,878 --> 01:06:08,297
No, he is a monster!

1347
01:06:08,380 --> 01:06:10,091
He belongs in prison!

1348
01:06:10,174 --> 01:06:13,886
Did you actually see him kill her?

1349
01:06:15,221 --> 01:06:17,181
Even if I didn't,

1350
01:06:18,015 --> 01:06:21,936
he's still the killer...

1351
01:06:35,157 --> 01:06:37,869
You really believe in Cho Dong-oh?

1352
01:06:37,952 --> 01:06:39,870
I believe
he didn't kill Lee Min-a.

1353
01:06:46,001 --> 01:06:48,837
All those are unsolved cases.

1354
01:06:50,923 --> 01:06:52,925
I'm sure you've heard of them.

1355
01:06:53,842 --> 01:06:57,054
Every victim was
brutally murdered.

1356
01:06:57,638 --> 01:07:00,307
I'm convinced it's the same guy.

1357
01:07:01,392 --> 01:07:04,520
And you think it's Cho Dong-oh?

1358
01:07:05,020 --> 01:07:05,479
Yes.

1359
01:07:05,562 --> 01:07:06,689
Based on what evidence?

1360
01:07:06,772 --> 01:07:08,024
There is none.

1361
01:07:08,107 --> 01:07:09,441
What?

1362
01:07:10,901 --> 01:07:13,446
He had that look in his eyes.

1363
01:07:13,529 --> 01:07:16,365
When you know someone's guilty
but can't prove it,

1364
01:07:16,448 --> 01:07:18,158
it drives you insane.

1365
01:07:18,784 --> 01:07:23,247
He looked at me with those eyes,
like he knew that.

1366
01:07:23,914 --> 01:07:26,041
The weirdest thing is,

1367
01:07:27,501 --> 01:07:29,962
every time someone died,

1368
01:07:30,045 --> 01:07:33,090
his family got beaten up
that same day.

1369
01:07:33,173 --> 01:07:34,926
He assaulted them.

1370
01:07:35,009 --> 01:07:38,888
And those records,
they're all in the precinct log.

1371
01:07:38,971 --> 01:07:41,265
Those logs became his alibi.

1372
01:07:42,683 --> 01:07:44,393
Isn't that weird?

1373
01:07:54,153 --> 01:07:56,155
The lab results came in
on Kang Chang-su's hammer.

1374
01:07:56,238 --> 01:07:59,074
It matched Lee Min-a's DNA.

1375
01:08:07,708 --> 01:08:08,501
Hello.

1376
01:08:08,584 --> 01:08:10,211
How have you been?

1377
01:08:10,294 --> 01:08:12,338
So, when do you think
I can get out?

1378
01:08:12,421 --> 01:08:13,839
- Mr. Cho Dong-oh.
- Yes?

1379
01:08:14,465 --> 01:08:16,008
- Sit down.
- Sure.

1380
01:08:17,676 --> 01:08:19,428
You came alone today?

1381
01:08:26,477 --> 01:08:28,062
What are these?

1382
01:08:31,690 --> 01:08:32,941
Do you know these women?

1383
01:08:33,025 --> 01:08:33,941
No.

1384
01:08:35,611 --> 01:08:36,612
You do.

1385
01:08:36,695 --> 01:08:37,780
What?

1386
01:08:38,697 --> 01:08:42,117
What's with you?

1387
01:08:46,080 --> 01:08:47,456
Did you kill them?

1388
01:08:48,290 --> 01:08:50,293
What's this all about?

1389
01:08:50,376 --> 01:08:51,334
Why did you kill them?

1390
01:08:51,418 --> 01:08:53,045
I told you, I don't know them!

1391
01:08:53,128 --> 01:08:54,255
Then why?

1392
01:08:54,338 --> 01:08:55,631
Sergeant!

1393
01:08:57,383 --> 01:08:58,842
Did you date them?

1394
01:09:02,888 --> 01:09:04,098
Kill them because you couldn't?

1395
01:09:04,181 --> 01:09:07,101
Sergeant, I already told you
everything last time!

1396
01:09:07,184 --> 01:09:08,978
- You liked them!
- Stop it...

1397
01:09:09,061 --> 01:09:12,606
But they rejected you,
so you killed them.

1398
01:09:12,689 --> 01:09:13,357
Right?

1399
01:09:13,440 --> 01:09:15,985
I don't know
what Det. Oh told you...

1400
01:09:16,068 --> 01:09:17,611
You didn't date Lee Min-a, right?

1401
01:09:17,694 --> 01:09:18,279
What?

1402
01:09:18,362 --> 01:09:20,823
Why'd a girl like her
ever be with filth like you?

1403
01:09:20,906 --> 01:09:21,907
Right?

1404
01:09:25,744 --> 01:09:27,704
Then why didn't you kill her?

1405
01:09:32,292 --> 01:09:35,129
That's why you had no alibi!

1406
01:09:35,212 --> 01:09:37,423
That's exactly why!

1407
01:09:38,298 --> 01:09:42,177
You didn't make an alibi
like the others!

1408
01:09:42,803 --> 01:09:46,598
Answer me, am I right?
You filthy prick.

1409
01:09:55,691 --> 01:09:58,068
Do you even know
what Det. Oh's problem is?

1410
01:09:58,819 --> 01:10:01,738
He's a coward.

1411
01:10:02,739 --> 01:10:06,118
He was worried I might
hurt his family,

1412
01:10:06,200 --> 01:10:07,787
so he locked me up here.

1413
01:10:07,870 --> 01:10:11,874
He did every vile thing he could,
that pathetic little crap.

1414
01:10:12,666 --> 01:10:19,089
If you don't mess with me,
I don't mess with you.

1415
01:10:23,719 --> 01:10:26,138
(My daughter)

1416
01:10:28,265 --> 01:10:29,850
Your daughter?

1417
01:10:30,726 --> 01:10:32,060
Daughter?

1418
01:10:33,187 --> 01:10:36,816
Looks like she misses her dad.

1419
01:10:36,899 --> 01:10:38,651
Is she pretty?

1420
01:10:38,734 --> 01:10:39,610
What?

1421
01:10:40,444 --> 01:10:41,445
Slim?

1422
01:10:43,030 --> 01:10:44,782
I hope she has long legs.

1423
01:10:44,865 --> 01:10:46,325
You got a death wish?

1424
01:10:50,579 --> 01:10:54,374
Thank you for finding
the real killer.

1425
01:10:58,420 --> 01:10:59,505
Officer!

1426
01:11:09,598 --> 01:11:11,725
As Exhibit 1, we submit the hammer

1427
01:11:11,807 --> 01:11:14,145
used in the crime
by the defendant.

1428
01:11:14,228 --> 01:11:17,148
The court accepts it.
Prosecutor, you may proceed.

1429
01:11:17,231 --> 01:11:19,566
As Exhibit 2,
we submit CCTV footages

1430
01:11:19,650 --> 01:11:21,861
showing the defendant's vehicle,

1431
01:11:21,944 --> 01:11:24,863
near the scene prior to
the time of the crime.

1432
01:11:25,572 --> 01:11:27,908
As Exhibit 3, we submit
the victim's talisman

1433
01:11:27,990 --> 01:11:30,453
found on the defendant at arrest.

1434
01:11:30,536 --> 01:11:32,246
It has already been confirmed
to be the same.

1435
01:11:36,542 --> 01:11:39,128
Hand over all
the unsolved case files?

1436
01:11:39,211 --> 01:11:40,587
Every single one.

1437
01:11:41,171 --> 01:11:42,089
All of it.

1438
01:11:42,172 --> 01:11:43,548
Why should I?

1439
01:11:43,632 --> 01:11:46,760
So that Cho can be locked up again
when he gets out.

1440
01:11:46,843 --> 01:11:48,595
You let him go.

1441
01:11:49,221 --> 01:11:50,639
Now you want to catch him again?

1442
01:11:50,722 --> 01:11:54,059
You wanted to catch him.
No, you said he must be caught.

1443
01:11:54,142 --> 01:11:55,311
Do I look like a pushover?

1444
01:11:55,394 --> 01:11:59,523
How do you catch a guy
with zero evidence?

1445
01:11:59,606 --> 01:12:01,566
Why do you think I...

1446
01:12:03,986 --> 01:12:05,237
We catch him with evidence.

1447
01:12:05,320 --> 01:12:07,948
How exactly will you find
that evidence?

1448
01:12:08,031 --> 01:12:10,659
Let's look for it together,
until our eyes bleed.

1449
01:12:10,742 --> 01:12:12,369
Are you messing with me?

1450
01:12:12,452 --> 01:12:14,746
It's not like that,
I'm serious.

1451
01:12:16,582 --> 01:12:18,042
- What now?
- I'm sorry.

1452
01:12:18,124 --> 01:12:19,834
- What's with you?
- Help me out.

1453
01:12:20,377 --> 01:12:23,756
Yeah, I know kneeling like this
is a bit over the top.

1454
01:12:23,839 --> 01:12:24,548
Fine, get up.

1455
01:12:24,631 --> 01:12:28,844
If I can earn your trust,
I'll do whatever it takes!

1456
01:12:28,927 --> 01:12:29,720
There's no need...

1457
01:12:29,803 --> 01:12:31,722
- Just watch my determination!
- Get the hell up, man!

1458
01:12:31,805 --> 01:12:33,098
I'll catch Cho Dong-oh
with this resolve!

1459
01:12:33,181 --> 01:12:34,099
Guys.

1460
01:12:34,182 --> 01:12:36,267
- Do something!
- Don't go! Please!

1461
01:12:36,351 --> 01:12:37,645
We're on the same team now!

1462
01:12:37,728 --> 01:12:39,980
I want to catch him too,
we're on the same team now!

1463
01:12:40,063 --> 01:12:41,482
- I'll lock him up!
- Fine, fine!

1464
01:12:41,565 --> 01:12:42,983
I know discipline inside out,

1465
01:12:43,066 --> 01:12:44,401
I'll make sure
you don't get dinged.

1466
01:12:44,484 --> 01:12:46,278
Fine! Just let go already!

1467
01:12:46,361 --> 01:12:48,948
I'll put Cho behind bars again!

1468
01:12:49,031 --> 01:12:50,449
I'm sorry!

1469
01:12:52,534 --> 01:12:56,163
These are the three most likely
cases linked to Cho.

1470
01:12:57,080 --> 01:12:59,208
He's extremely meticulous.

1471
01:12:59,291 --> 01:13:01,126
We went through everything
around him,

1472
01:13:01,209 --> 01:13:04,338
not a single thing worth calling
a trophy was found.

1473
01:13:05,047 --> 01:13:09,343
No victim's underwear,
ring, hairpin, button...

1474
01:13:09,426 --> 01:13:12,012
even body parts like teeth.

1475
01:13:12,095 --> 01:13:15,807
So, none of the victims'
personal items were found.

1476
01:13:17,809 --> 01:13:20,228
This could be a coincidence,

1477
01:13:20,729 --> 01:13:23,524
but there's a missing item
from the first victim.

1478
01:13:23,607 --> 01:13:25,150
The brown hairband.

1479
01:13:25,233 --> 01:13:29,529
And a similar item was found
on the second victim.

1480
01:13:30,197 --> 01:13:34,493
Among the second victim's
missing items was a white bra.

1481
01:13:35,369 --> 01:13:38,789
- The third victim...
- Had the same white bra!

1482
01:13:38,872 --> 01:13:42,249
So he leaves the previous
victim's items with the next one?

1483
01:13:43,001 --> 01:13:44,837
Could that be Cho Dong-oh's MO?

1484
01:13:44,920 --> 01:13:45,504
Right!

1485
01:13:45,587 --> 01:13:46,797
Don't get too excited.

1486
01:13:46,880 --> 01:13:49,258
You think we wouldn't
have noticed that?

1487
01:13:49,341 --> 01:13:51,552
Brown hairband? White bra?

1488
01:13:51,635 --> 01:13:53,637
Ask any woman on the street,

1489
01:13:53,720 --> 01:13:57,432
they'll have one of the two,
it's too common to be evidence.

1490
01:13:57,516 --> 01:14:03,147
And nothing's reported
missing from the third victim yet.

1491
01:14:03,230 --> 01:14:05,941
Even if something's gone,
the family might not know.

1492
01:14:06,566 --> 01:14:09,111
Then if even one of those items

1493
01:14:09,194 --> 01:14:11,488
is in Cho Dong-oh's possession...

1494
01:14:11,571 --> 01:14:13,407
Game over.

1495
01:14:13,490 --> 01:14:15,784
That's so obvious.

1496
01:14:15,867 --> 01:14:17,911
Don't be so dramatic.

1497
01:14:17,994 --> 01:14:19,204
These idiots.

1498
01:14:19,287 --> 01:14:21,415
Why are you being pissy?

1499
01:14:21,498 --> 01:14:23,626
Anyway, I know it's annoying,

1500
01:14:23,709 --> 01:14:26,670
but check if anything's missing
from the victim's belongings.

1501
01:15:17,888 --> 01:15:19,473
I kept quiet...

1502
01:15:24,978 --> 01:15:27,272
I, I cleaned everything.

1503
01:15:32,694 --> 01:15:33,945
Let's eat.

1504
01:15:38,825 --> 01:15:39,868
Where's Cho Dong-oh?

1505
01:15:39,950 --> 01:15:41,453
He just went in.

1506
01:15:45,624 --> 01:15:49,252
Psalm 20:5...
my... my Lord...

1507
01:15:49,961 --> 01:15:54,091
I pray to You...

1508
01:15:54,173 --> 01:15:57,845
Can we catch him just by
staking out like this?

1509
01:15:57,928 --> 01:16:00,722
Staking out is basic police work,
didn't you know that?

1510
01:16:02,724 --> 01:16:04,726
He won't act rashly, right?

1511
01:16:05,227 --> 01:16:09,105
He's cautious,
he won't make a move easily.

1512
01:16:21,993 --> 01:16:23,578
- What are you doing?
- What?

1513
01:16:25,038 --> 01:16:26,498
Not going to pray?

1514
01:16:28,917 --> 01:16:31,044
Lord and Father, thank you.

1515
01:16:32,087 --> 01:16:35,841
Thank you for giving us
our daily bread.

1516
01:16:35,923 --> 01:16:37,050
Young-hee.

1517
01:16:39,719 --> 01:16:42,973
Why did you tell
useless stuff to the cops?

1518
01:16:47,519 --> 01:16:49,020
You thought I wouldn't notice?

1519
01:16:50,605 --> 01:16:52,148
Come here, come here!

1520
01:16:52,858 --> 01:16:53,859
- Son of a...
- You deserve a beating!

1521
01:16:53,941 --> 01:16:54,568
Stay put!

1522
01:16:54,651 --> 01:16:56,862
Things will get messy
if he finds out about the bug.

1523
01:16:56,945 --> 01:16:58,530
Is that really
the issue right now?

1524
01:16:58,613 --> 01:17:00,198
Why is there no sound?

1525
01:17:05,954 --> 01:17:07,956
Goddamn jerk!

1526
01:17:10,458 --> 01:17:11,709
I'll go inside!

1527
01:17:12,711 --> 01:17:14,171
Ye-sol, are you okay?

1528
01:17:14,254 --> 01:17:15,172
Are you hurt?

1529
01:17:15,255 --> 01:17:16,548
Are you insane?

1530
01:17:16,631 --> 01:17:18,467
Are you out of your mind?

1531
01:17:18,550 --> 01:17:20,010
- You dirty wench!
- Cho Dong-oh!

1532
01:17:22,137 --> 01:17:23,054
You jerk!

1533
01:17:24,139 --> 01:17:25,599
Are you even human?

1534
01:17:26,975 --> 01:17:28,101
Are you alright?

1535
01:17:28,810 --> 01:17:30,312
Mom...

1536
01:17:32,355 --> 01:17:33,148
Hey.

1537
01:17:33,231 --> 01:17:36,318
Shouldn't you ask me that?

1538
01:17:38,445 --> 01:17:40,822
You pricks...

1539
01:17:41,823 --> 01:17:43,492
You know this is illegal, right?

1540
01:17:43,575 --> 01:17:45,243
You think I'll just stay quiet?

1541
01:17:45,869 --> 01:17:47,704
Call 911, prick.

1542
01:18:08,350 --> 01:18:09,601
What happened here?

1543
01:18:09,684 --> 01:18:11,353
Well, it's just...

1544
01:18:11,436 --> 01:18:13,772
Cho Dong-oh accused you of

1545
01:18:13,855 --> 01:18:15,815
illegal wiretapping
and trespassing.

1546
01:18:17,400 --> 01:18:18,485
Let's talk outside.

1547
01:18:31,998 --> 01:18:34,001
Step aside on this case for now.

1548
01:18:34,084 --> 01:18:34,668
Ma'am!

1549
01:18:34,751 --> 01:18:36,670
If you don't want to
get demoted again,

1550
01:18:36,753 --> 01:18:38,880
you better listen to me.

1551
01:18:51,726 --> 01:18:52,352
Hmm?

1552
01:18:52,435 --> 01:18:53,895
You were right.

1553
01:18:54,479 --> 01:18:57,065
There was a missing item
from the third victim.

1554
01:18:57,148 --> 01:18:57,774
What?

1555
01:18:57,857 --> 01:18:59,985
She has a matching ring
with her boyfriend

1556
01:19:00,068 --> 01:19:02,154
that her family even didn't know.

1557
01:19:02,237 --> 01:19:06,032
A silver ring with her initials
engraved in alphabet.

1558
01:19:06,615 --> 01:19:09,786
Finding that would be
airtight evidence.

1559
01:19:17,877 --> 01:19:19,504
Mr. Cho Dong-oh.

1560
01:19:20,130 --> 01:19:22,298
Do you even realize
what's happening?

1561
01:19:23,758 --> 01:19:26,636
You think you're free
and this is all over?

1562
01:19:27,345 --> 01:19:28,555
Who are you?

1563
01:19:29,639 --> 01:19:31,307
The prosecutor who freed you.

1564
01:19:31,391 --> 01:19:34,561
Wasn't it fun hanging out
with the Gangnam PD boys?

1565
01:19:36,396 --> 01:19:38,565
From now on,
I'll be looking into you,

1566
01:19:38,648 --> 01:19:40,816
you'll have your hands full.

1567
01:19:40,900 --> 01:19:42,736
I'm a little crazy too.

1568
01:19:49,242 --> 01:19:50,452
Mr. Cho.

1569
01:19:51,369 --> 01:19:54,289
Have you ever been
loved in your life?

1570
01:19:55,540 --> 01:19:57,584
Whether it's Lee Min-a,
or Lee Jin-kyung?

1571
01:20:00,712 --> 01:20:03,298
I know guys like you,

1572
01:20:04,507 --> 01:20:07,427
you're just pitiful.

1573
01:20:07,510 --> 01:20:10,764
You hear me? A pitiful prick.

1574
01:20:20,440 --> 01:20:23,276
See you soon, and get well.

1575
01:20:26,905 --> 01:20:28,656
I do not rejoice in sin.

1576
01:20:29,865 --> 01:20:31,034
I...

1577
01:20:33,703 --> 01:20:36,832
Can you hear my voice?

1578
01:20:36,915 --> 01:20:38,291
Ma'am.

1579
01:20:38,374 --> 01:20:41,461
Can I just check your ring?

1580
01:20:42,420 --> 01:20:43,254
Yes.

1581
01:20:52,430 --> 01:20:53,598
Thank you.

1582
01:20:58,061 --> 01:21:00,939
May I take a look at the Bible?

1583
01:21:01,022 --> 01:21:02,858
No, I'll get in trouble!

1584
01:21:02,941 --> 01:21:04,401
Just a quick look, I promise!

1585
01:21:04,484 --> 01:21:04,776
No.

1586
01:21:04,859 --> 01:21:07,154
- One quick look!
- I'll get in trouble!

1587
01:21:07,237 --> 01:21:09,072
One moment, I'll be quick.

1588
01:21:10,406 --> 01:21:13,577
This was where your husband
hid women's belongings, right?

1589
01:21:13,660 --> 01:21:14,994
I don't know...

1590
01:21:45,900 --> 01:21:48,820
(The Nest)

1591
01:22:14,304 --> 01:22:15,889
It fits well.

1592
01:22:17,891 --> 01:22:19,684
Do you feel good?

1593
01:22:20,517 --> 01:22:23,396
How would it feel to die
to someone like me?

1594
01:22:26,858 --> 01:22:29,444
What do you think?

1595
01:22:31,029 --> 01:22:32,572
How would you feel?

1596
01:22:35,700 --> 01:22:37,785
What's with your look?

1597
01:22:38,661 --> 01:22:39,454
Hey!

1598
01:22:41,414 --> 01:22:43,458
It's no fun
if you don't get excited.

1599
01:22:44,584 --> 01:22:45,584
Wench!

1600
01:22:46,294 --> 01:22:48,838
You're going to die anyway,
scream a little.

1601
01:22:49,339 --> 01:22:51,048
I'll make it fun for you.

1602
01:22:54,010 --> 01:22:55,678
Mr. Cho Dong-oh...

1603
01:22:57,180 --> 01:22:58,097
What?

1604
01:22:59,474 --> 01:23:01,184
You did good.

1605
01:23:05,855 --> 01:23:07,065
What did you say?

1606
01:23:09,108 --> 01:23:10,068
The ring...

1607
01:23:10,151 --> 01:23:12,445
My husband took it...

1608
01:23:12,528 --> 01:23:13,238
Pardon?

1609
01:23:13,321 --> 01:23:16,532
The day before
the police took him,

1610
01:23:17,867 --> 01:23:20,328
he snatched it from me.

1611
01:23:21,120 --> 01:23:25,542
Cho took it before
the police raided him.

1612
01:23:25,624 --> 01:23:27,209
The only place
he could have hidden

1613
01:23:27,293 --> 01:23:28,753
the ring is the Nest, right?

1614
01:23:28,836 --> 01:23:31,631
What if he says it's not his?

1615
01:23:33,132 --> 01:23:35,385
The moment he touches the ring,

1616
01:23:35,468 --> 01:23:38,889
snap the cuffs on him,
and it's game over.

1617
01:23:38,972 --> 01:23:40,431
Shall I do it?

1618
01:23:41,182 --> 01:23:42,100
Do what?

1619
01:23:43,977 --> 01:23:45,228
I knew you'd do this...

1620
01:23:45,311 --> 01:23:47,272
Couldn't resist,
you murderous prick!

1621
01:23:48,022 --> 01:23:49,399
Ma'am, are you okay?

1622
01:23:49,482 --> 01:23:51,526
- Did you film everything?
- Yeah, I got it all.

1623
01:23:51,609 --> 01:23:52,819
Hey, drop the knife.

1624
01:23:52,901 --> 01:23:54,279
Drop the knife,
or I'll shoot you!

1625
01:23:54,362 --> 01:23:55,280
Get down!

1626
01:23:55,363 --> 01:23:56,406
On the floor!

1627
01:24:01,744 --> 01:24:03,830
The first one is always a blank!

1628
01:24:07,249 --> 01:24:09,628
You son of a gun!
Put the knife down!

1629
01:24:09,711 --> 01:24:11,129
You're going to kill again?

1630
01:24:11,212 --> 01:24:14,257
Why am I the killer?
I didn't kill Lee Min-a.

1631
01:24:15,048 --> 01:24:17,468
I was wrongfully imprisoned.

1632
01:24:18,052 --> 01:24:21,264
It'll be over soon. Just wait.

1633
01:24:54,672 --> 01:24:55,590
Please help...

1634
01:24:55,673 --> 01:24:56,423
Dammit.

1635
01:25:20,865 --> 01:25:22,200
You were going to kill her.

1636
01:25:22,283 --> 01:25:24,911
And you killed other women too!

1637
01:25:24,994 --> 01:25:27,372
Holy Christ, you're so strong!

1638
01:25:27,455 --> 01:25:29,082
Look at this guy!

1639
01:25:29,165 --> 01:25:30,708
- Let's talk this out, okay?
- Sir!

1640
01:25:34,170 --> 01:25:35,338
Where's my gun?

1641
01:25:36,339 --> 01:25:37,798
Ma'am, are you okay?

1642
01:25:38,548 --> 01:25:39,425
Hey!

1643
01:25:40,258 --> 01:25:42,012
Go catch that jerk first.

1644
01:25:42,095 --> 01:25:43,096
Okay.

1645
01:25:56,275 --> 01:25:57,901
- Sir!
- Catch up!

1646
01:26:06,327 --> 01:26:07,662
Cover the top.

1647
01:26:14,001 --> 01:26:15,169
Dong-oh.

1648
01:26:17,880 --> 01:26:19,423
Cho Dong-oh.

1649
01:26:19,966 --> 01:26:21,383
It's all over.

1650
01:26:22,218 --> 01:26:24,387
I got the entire force outside.

1651
01:26:34,772 --> 01:26:37,900
Come out now, and I'll let
the whole knife thing slide.

1652
01:26:50,788 --> 01:26:51,581
Dammit!

1653
01:27:04,635 --> 01:27:05,386
Goddamn...

1654
01:27:05,928 --> 01:27:07,054
Goddamn prick...

1655
01:27:20,735 --> 01:27:21,944
Piece of crap...

1656
01:27:35,208 --> 01:27:36,584
You son of a gun!

1657
01:27:37,334 --> 01:27:38,336
Get up!

1658
01:27:42,089 --> 01:27:43,673
Sir, are you okay?

1659
01:27:45,468 --> 01:27:46,469
Sir!

1660
01:27:46,552 --> 01:27:47,678
Block him!

1661
01:27:50,848 --> 01:27:51,807
Why you...

1662
01:28:02,485 --> 01:28:04,153
You little piece of crap!

1663
01:28:06,197 --> 01:28:07,156
Damn!

1664
01:28:17,291 --> 01:28:18,251
Dammit...

1665
01:28:25,800 --> 01:28:29,053
Cho Dong-oh,
you're under arrest for murder.

1666
01:28:29,136 --> 01:28:32,348
You have the right to
an attorney and also have...

1667
01:28:38,312 --> 01:28:41,899
Arrest me, I dare you!

1668
01:28:57,707 --> 01:29:00,459
Joong-ho, you idiot!

1669
01:29:01,752 --> 01:29:05,006
Hey! You okay?

1670
01:29:05,089 --> 01:29:05,965
I feel like I'm going to die...

1671
01:29:06,048 --> 01:29:07,633
What the hell?

1672
01:29:09,010 --> 01:29:10,720
Let me see.

1673
01:29:11,387 --> 01:29:12,346
You idiot.

1674
01:29:14,765 --> 01:29:16,851
Cho Dong-oh, you jerk!

1675
01:29:17,435 --> 01:29:18,144
Hey!

1676
01:29:22,106 --> 01:29:24,358
I'm sorry, I'm a little late...

1677
01:29:26,110 --> 01:29:31,407
Ma'am, he's been stabbed...

1678
01:29:33,618 --> 01:29:35,745
Here, put pressure.

1679
01:29:36,329 --> 01:29:38,206
Oh my gosh! Joong-ho!

1680
01:29:38,289 --> 01:29:39,958
Stay with me, stay with me!

1681
01:29:40,041 --> 01:29:41,209
Breathe!

1682
01:29:41,292 --> 01:29:44,503
Call an ambulance!
Ambulance!

1683
01:29:45,421 --> 01:29:47,298
Stay awake, man!

1684
01:29:50,217 --> 01:29:51,010
Buddy...

1685
01:29:53,929 --> 01:29:55,181
What are you doing?

1686
01:29:55,264 --> 01:29:58,517
When else in life
will I get stabbed with a knife?

1687
01:30:00,061 --> 01:30:01,270
What a lunatic.

1688
01:30:02,855 --> 01:30:04,524
This guy is so weird.

1689
01:30:04,607 --> 01:30:06,276
Ow! I'm injured!

1690
01:30:06,359 --> 01:30:07,901
Sorry about that.

1691
01:30:09,487 --> 01:30:11,281
Look at this blood!

1692
01:30:11,364 --> 01:30:13,240
Call the ambulance!

1693
01:30:13,324 --> 01:30:15,075
Let's get a move on.

1694
01:30:17,078 --> 01:30:19,497
Get in there,
we got you good.

1695
01:30:26,379 --> 01:30:27,922
Are you okay?

1696
01:30:28,005 --> 01:30:29,215
No...

1697
01:30:29,298 --> 01:30:30,425
He's not going to die, right?

1698
01:30:30,508 --> 01:30:32,510
The wound isn't as deep
as it looks.

1699
01:30:33,260 --> 01:30:34,553
Let's move.

1700
01:30:36,514 --> 01:30:38,349
You're going with him?

1701
01:30:38,432 --> 01:30:41,394
Yeah... same direction.

1702
01:30:41,477 --> 01:30:43,438
Same direction to where?

1703
01:30:43,521 --> 01:30:46,982
Ma'am, never do that again.

1704
01:30:47,983 --> 01:30:50,236
Who uses the prosecutor
as a bait?

1705
01:30:50,778 --> 01:30:54,282
It was her idea.
Don't be a brat.

1706
01:30:54,365 --> 01:30:55,950
She almost got killed...

1707
01:30:56,033 --> 01:30:59,537
It's okay, I'm healthy,
let's get a move on!

1708
01:31:01,122 --> 01:31:02,624
I have to go to the hospital too...

1709
01:31:02,707 --> 01:31:04,041
Excuse me!

1710
01:31:11,257 --> 01:31:12,466
Seo Jae-hyuk!

1711
01:31:12,967 --> 01:31:13,926
Hey.

1712
01:31:14,008 --> 01:31:15,928
Why are you here
all by yourself?

1713
01:31:17,096 --> 01:31:18,973
They all just left...

1714
01:31:19,056 --> 01:31:20,682
You seem perfectly fine.

1715
01:31:20,766 --> 01:31:23,061
Were you hiding in the corner
while your partner got stabbed?

1716
01:31:23,144 --> 01:31:26,064
What are you saying?
I got hurt way more.

1717
01:31:26,147 --> 01:31:27,982
I practically caught the guy.

1718
01:31:28,065 --> 01:31:31,986
Two cops couldn't take down
a civilian and got us out?

1719
01:31:32,069 --> 01:31:35,782
You guys couldn't do anything,
so I had to catch him.

1720
01:31:35,865 --> 01:31:38,909
And you released the guy
we locked away!

1721
01:31:39,452 --> 01:31:42,747
You caught him in a weird way!

1722
01:31:43,998 --> 01:31:45,166
Good work.

1723
01:31:45,666 --> 01:31:46,667
You too.

1724
01:31:49,712 --> 01:31:53,800
Certificate of appointment,
Sgt. Seo Jae-hyuk, Boeun PD,

1725
01:31:53,883 --> 01:31:55,176
promoted to lieutenant.

1726
01:31:57,928 --> 01:31:59,638
Congrats, sir!

1727
01:32:00,639 --> 01:32:02,307
Congratulations!

1728
01:32:02,391 --> 01:32:05,102
Second time as lieutenant,
a bit embarrassing.

1729
01:32:06,187 --> 01:32:07,146
Hey!

1730
01:32:07,229 --> 01:32:08,731
What's happening with him?

1731
01:32:08,814 --> 01:32:11,234
I'll pretend I didn't
receive that order.

1732
01:32:11,316 --> 01:32:12,276
What do you mean?

1733
01:32:12,359 --> 01:32:16,322
“One may refuse an unlawful order
without consequence.”

1734
01:32:16,405 --> 01:32:19,242
Article 57 of the National
Public Service Act was changed.

1735
01:32:19,325 --> 01:32:21,452
You said you'd get
him to quit first.

1736
01:32:22,411 --> 01:32:23,705
Alright, let's take a photo!

1737
01:32:23,788 --> 01:32:24,997
Photo time!

1738
01:32:25,080 --> 01:32:28,251
My team, over here!
Stand beside him!

1739
01:32:28,334 --> 01:32:30,378
Make sure the chief looks good!

1740
01:32:30,461 --> 01:32:32,630
One, two, three!

1741
01:32:34,507 --> 01:32:36,883
- Congratulations!
- Congratulations!

1742
01:32:38,469 --> 01:32:40,554
Hey, what about you?

1743
01:32:51,232 --> 01:32:52,775
I heard this is the cheapest one!

1744
01:32:52,858 --> 01:32:54,651
It's got 50 installments left!

1745
01:32:57,154 --> 01:32:58,447
Yong-man!

1746
01:33:00,407 --> 01:33:02,325
Are you the one
who messed with my partner?

1747
01:33:02,409 --> 01:33:03,619
It wasn't me.

1748
01:33:04,954 --> 01:33:06,706
Welcome, welcome,
come on in!

1749
01:33:06,789 --> 01:33:08,415
Son of a gun!

1750
01:33:12,962 --> 01:33:15,464
Goddammit! You little crap!

1751
01:33:17,341 --> 01:33:19,927
He punched my balls!
My balls!

1752
01:33:42,032 --> 01:33:43,409
(Bae Seong-woo)

1753
01:33:43,492 --> 01:33:46,245
Underestimate Capoeira,
and you're dead.

1754
01:33:46,912 --> 01:33:48,539
(Jung Ga-ram)

1755
01:33:50,457 --> 01:33:53,711
I can't return those feelings.

1756
01:33:54,962 --> 01:33:56,422
(Esom)

1757
01:33:56,505 --> 01:33:59,258
I'll make sure to catch the guy!

1758
01:33:59,341 --> 01:34:01,176
All right! Let go of me!

1759
01:34:02,219 --> 01:34:03,596
(Cho Han Cheul)

1760
01:34:03,679 --> 01:34:06,724
Because... I'm married!

1761
01:34:07,557 --> 01:34:09,101
(Yoon Kyung Ho)

1762
01:34:12,897 --> 01:34:14,940
(Directed by
Park Cheol-hwan)

1763
01:34:16,066 --> 01:34:20,446
(The Ultimate Duo)
